window.COURSE_PAPERS = (window.COURSE_PAPERS || []).concat([{"kind":"p1","id":"DP2013","title":"Paper 01 · 2013 specimen","time":90,"intro":"<p><b>CAPE Digital Media Unit 1 Paper 01 · 2013 specimen</b> · 1 hour 30 minutes · 45 items</p><p class=\"hint\">Original: CAPE Digital Media Unit 1 specimen paper (2013).</p><ol><li>Answer <b>ALL</b> items. Each item has four options lettered (A), (B), (C), (D).</li><li>Start the optional timer to practise under exam conditions.</li><li>Submit to see your score, the key and an explanation for every item.</li></ol>","items":[{"q":"Which of the following BEST describes 'Digital Media'?","options":["Online broadcast medium","Social media content","Internet transmission data wired over limited network","Electronic content that can be transmitted over a computer network"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Digital media is content in electronic (digital) form that can be stored and transmitted over computer networks.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following does NOT refer to new media?","options":["Feature TV offered over the air broadcast","Community participation around media","Democratization of the creation, publishing and distribution of media tools","On demand access to content anytime, anywhere using any digital device"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Over-the-air broadcast TV is traditional (old) media; the others describe interactive, on-demand new media.","module":"1"},{"q":"Approximately, for how long have digital media been in existence?","options":["5 years","10 years","15 years","30 years"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Digital media date back to the spread of personal computers in the early 1980s, around 30 years before this paper.","module":"1"},{"q":"In the early days of digital media, 'advertising' was construed to mean","options":["the proliferation of websites","emergence of smart mobile devices","the proliferation of self-publishing platforms","message creation by electronic agencies"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Early digital advertising was seen as agencies creating messages electronically, before websites, smartphones and self-publishing spread.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following BEST describes 'local content'?","options":["Content that is not imported","Community owned and adapted knowledge","Indigenous content","Content for people in a certain locality"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Local content is commonly defined as the expression of the locally owned and adapted knowledge of a community.","module":"1"},{"q":"In terms of involvement in the digital revolution, the Caribbean Community can be characterized as","options":["exporters of content","users of local content","creators of local content","mostly consumers of imported content"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. The Caribbean mostly consumes digital content produced elsewhere rather than creating and exporting its own.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is used for media delivery?","options":["Mobile phone","Keyboard","Printer","Mouse"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. A mobile phone can receive and play media content; the keyboard and mouse are input devices.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is NOT a characteristic of digital media?","options":["Create connections","Create community","Foster dynamic dialogue","Produce permanent records"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Digital media are dynamic and easily changed, connecting people and fostering dialogue rather than producing fixed permanent records.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is a pitfall of digital media?","options":["Boost brand","Encourage too much follow up","Create ethical issues in discovery","Stabilise the value of resources"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Digital media can raise ethical problems, such as privacy and copyright issues, which is a pitfall; boosting a brand is a benefit.","module":"1"},{"q":"The source of intellectual property can be traced to","options":["conferred authority","creation of the mind","inherited liability","shared effort"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Intellectual property refers to creations of the mind, such as inventions, designs and artistic works.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is MOST likely to raise ethical issues associated with digital media?","options":["Sharing a personal video production","Playing a rented DVD","Stripping of a DRM protected track","Downloading a Linux distribution movie using bittorrent"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Removing DRM protection bypasses the copyright owner's controls, which raises ethical and legal issues.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following businesses uses the long-tail business model?","options":["Apple iTunes","NBC Universal","Caribbean Sports Wear","Website development firm"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. iTunes sells huge numbers of niche items in small quantities online, which is the long-tail model.","module":"1"},{"q":"The open movement does NOT include open","options":["standards","access movement","source movement","software initiative"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Open standards, open access and open source are parts of the open movement; 'open software initiative' is not a recognised part (it is the Open Source Initiative).","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is a multimedia software tool?","options":["Eclipse","Audacity","Microsoft Word","Google Chrome"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Audacity is an audio editing tool; Eclipse is a programming IDE, Word a word processor and Chrome a browser.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following are digital media platforms?<br>I. Satellite<br>II. Internet<br>III. 3D art","options":["I and II only","I and III only","II and III only","I, II and III"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Satellite and the Internet are platforms that deliver digital media; 3D art is a type of content, not a platform.","module":"1"},{"q":"A 'digital native' is an individual who","options":["uses technology without difficulty","repairs and maintains computers and servers","was born before the existence of digital technology","was born during the proliferation of digital technology"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. A digital native is someone born into the digital age, growing up with digital technology around them.","module":"2"},{"q":"A 'digital immigrant' is an individual who","options":["has adopted digital technology in later life","has moved away from digital technology","was born before the existence of digital technology","applies the principles of software development"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. A digital immigrant was born before the digital age and adopted digital technology later in life.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following BEST describes the 'digital media ecosystem' concept?","options":["An online library","A government information service","A business and corporate communications system","Media based on human communication, and shared electronically"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. The digital media ecosystem is the interconnected system of human communication that is created and shared electronically.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following BEST describes the digital convergence?","options":["A document domain","An interpersonal domain","A global system of computer networks","Consolidation of multiple communication technologies"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Digital convergence is the merging of different technologies, such as phone, camera and computer, into one device or platform.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following BEST describes the term 'Internet'?","options":["Locally designed connectivity","Group of unconnected websites","Global computer network","System of stand-alone-computers"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. The Internet is a global network of interconnected computer networks.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following BEST describes the concept of digital media communication?","options":["Personal reflection","Static online communication","Face-to-face communication","Interactive, online communication"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Digital media communication is interactive and takes place online.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is NOT a form of digital media?","options":["E-books","Live streaming","Feature filmshow","Electronic online services"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. A feature film show in a cinema is traditional media; e-books, streaming and online services are digital.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is NOT part of the digital media value chain?","options":["Single site service","Content creation","Content distribution","Customer management"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. The value chain covers creating, distributing and managing customers for content; 'single site service' is not a stage.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is a common work arrangement for digital media practitioners?","options":["Virtual team","Office team","Management team","Administrative team"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Digital media practitioners often work in virtual teams, collaborating online from different locations.","module":"2"},{"q":"Globalization is a process where an increased proportion of","options":["computer networking takes place","engagement takes place through social media","economic, social and cultural activities are carried out across national borders","economic, social and cultural activities are carried out within a country"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Globalization means more economic, social and cultural activity happens across national borders.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is a challenge in the digital media industry?","options":["Piracy","Convergence","Collaboration","Communication"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Piracy, the illegal copying and sharing of content, is a major challenge for the digital media industry.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is an example of debt funding?","options":["Loan","Crowd funding","Venture Capital","Angel investment"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. A loan is debt funding because it must be repaid; venture capital and angel investment are equity funding.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is a tool for generating ideas?","options":["Texting","Mind-mapping","Application development","PowerPoint presentation"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Mind-mapping visually links ideas, making it a useful idea-generation tool.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following BEST describes the purpose of a project proposal?","options":["To provide the budget","To introduce the team","To provide project data","To introduce the project"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. A project proposal introduces and outlines the project to stakeholders; the budget and team are only parts of it.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following are key aspects of a project proposal?","options":["Conclusion, reference","Apps, disks, computers","Text messages, blogs, web pages","Overview, target audience, budget"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. A proposal typically includes a project overview, the target audience and the budget.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following sequences describes the creative process?<br>I. Develop<br>II. Implement<br>III. Create","options":["I, II, III","II, I, III","II, III, I","III, I, II"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Ideas are first created, then developed, and finally implemented.","module":"3"},{"q":"At which stage in the creative process would a person need to describe the issue to be solved?","options":["Ideation","Analysis","Acceptance","Implementation"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. During analysis the problem is examined and described before ideas are generated.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following channels of communication does NOT belong to the digital age?","options":["Fax","Blog","Wiki","Email"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Fax is an older, analogue-era technology; blogs, wikis and email are digital-age channels.","module":"3"},{"q":"What type of implementation of the creative process does the diagram illustrate?","passage":"<p>Item 34 refers to the following diagram.</p><p><i>Diagram:</i> seven arrow shapes in a single row, each pointing to the next, left to right: Accept Situation → Analyse → Define → Ideate → Select → Implement → Evaluate.</p>","options":["Cyclic","Linear","Feedback","Selection"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. The stages follow one after another in a straight line with no loop back, so the process is linear.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following activities is missing from the group: creativity, innovation, concept development?","options":["Ideation","Problem definition","Problem solving","Brain storming"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Ideation sits with creativity, innovation and concept development as the idea-generating activities of the creative process.","module":"3"},{"q":"A writer has developed an outline for a story and has decided to follow it through. What is the next stage in the creative process that should be undertaken?","options":["Ideation","Selection","Acceptance","Implementation"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. The idea has already been chosen, so the next stage is implementation, actually carrying it out.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following tasks must be completed prior to the actual making of a digital media product?","options":["Production","Fact finding","Pre-production","Problem solving"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Pre-production (planning, scripting, storyboarding) must be finished before production begins.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following is a tool that can be used to edit photographs?","options":["Pixlr","Audacity","MovieMaker","Storyboard Pro"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Pixlr is an online photo editor; Audacity edits audio and MovieMaker edits video.","module":"3"},{"q":"Brainstorming, scriptwriting and storyboarding are part of","options":["ideation","production","pre-production","implementation"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Brainstorming, scripting and storyboarding are planning tasks carried out in pre-production.","module":"3"},{"q":"The diagram shown above is an illustration of","passage":"<p>Item 40 refers to the following diagram.</p><p><i>Diagram:</i> titled “Media Pre-Production Process”. A starburst labelled Brainstorm sits at the top. Below it four large downward arrows follow one another: Ideation → Writing → Pre-Visualization → Production Planning, ending in a box that reads: Script breakdown, Create shot list, Make shooting schedule, Make equipment lists. Bars down the sides label related tasks: Develop characters, settings, situations; Research; Develop themes/thesis; Storyboard; Scout locations; Assemble cast and crew.</p>","options":["ideation","scripting","production","pre-production"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. All the steps shown happen before filming begins, so the diagram shows the pre-production process.","module":"3"},{"q":"How many sections are formed when the lines are drawn in relation to the rule of thirds?","options":["Three","Six","Nine","Twelve"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Two horizontal and two vertical lines divide the frame into nine equal sections.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following groupings are elements of composition?","options":["Video and lighting","Audio and composition","Rule of thirds and lighting","Rule of thirds and psychology of colours"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. The rule of thirds and lighting both affect how a shot is composed.","module":"3"},{"q":"A teacher would like her students to recap a particular lesson, ask questions, add comments, add discussion points and post any additional resources. Which digital media tool is most suitable to complete this task?","options":["A blog","Instant messaging","Audio recording","Video conferencing"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. A blog lets the teacher post a recap while students comment, ask questions and share resources in one place.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following will allow a group of five persons staying at different locations to plan a presentation as a group project for a course?","options":["A wiki","Podcast","Live streaming","A Word processor"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. A wiki lets several people in different places edit and build shared content together.","module":"3"},{"q":"A couple is celebrating their fortieth wedding anniversary. Which of the following will BEST capture all aspects of the years they spent together?","options":["Photograph and video story","Video and audio story","Audio and photography story","Audio, photograph and video story"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Combining audio, photographs and video gives the richest multimedia record of their years together.","module":"3"}]},{"kind":"p1","id":"DPspec2018","title":"Paper 01 · 2018 CBT specimen","time":90,"intro":"<p><b>CAPE Digital Media Unit 1 Paper 01 · 2018 CBT specimen</b> · 1 hour 30 minutes · 45 items</p><p class=\"hint\">Original: CXC specimen paper 02159010/SPEC 2018 (computer-based), circulated as the 2020 specimen paper.</p><ol><li>Answer <b>ALL</b> items. Each item has four options lettered (A), (B), (C), (D).</li><li>Start the optional timer to practise under exam conditions.</li><li>Submit to see your score, the key and an explanation for every item.</li></ol><p class=\"tip\"><b>Printable version:</b> The fillable PDF of this paper, with a Submit button that scores it, is available to <a href=\"games/res/CAPE_DM_U1_Paper01_Exercise.pdf\" download>download (PDF, 8 pages)</a>. Its key matches the one used here except items 13, 32 and 42, which are under review; follow the explanations on this page.</p>","items":[{"q":"Which of the following BEST describes the term 'digital media'?","options":["Social media content","Online broadcast medium","Internet transmission data wired over limited network","Electronic content that can be transmitted over a computer network"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Digital media is content in electronic (digital) form that can be stored and transmitted over computer networks.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following does NOT refer to new media?","options":["Feature TV offered over the air broadcast","Community participation around media","Democratization of the creation, publishing and distribution of media tools","On demand access to content anytime, anywhere using any digital device"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Over-the-air TV broadcast is traditional media; new media is interactive, participatory and available on demand.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following BEST describes digital convergence?","options":["A document domain","An interpersonal domain","A global system of computer networks","Consolidation of multiple communication technologies"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Digital convergence is the merging of several communication technologies (text, audio, video, telephony) into one device or platform.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following phrases BEST describes the term 'Internet'?","options":["Global computer network","Group of unconnected websites","Locally designed connectivity","System of stand-alone computers"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. The Internet is a global network of interconnected computer networks.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following phrases BEST describes 'local content'?","options":["Indigenous content","Content that is not imported","Content for people in a certain locality","Community owned and adapted knowledge"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Local content is the expression of the locally owned and adapted knowledge of a community.","module":"1"},{"q":"In terms of involvement in the digital revolution, the Caribbean Community can be characterized as","options":["exporters of content","users of local content","creators of local content","mostly consumers of imported content"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. The Caribbean mostly consumes digital content produced elsewhere rather than creating and exporting its own.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is used for media delivery?","options":["Mobile phone","Keyboard","Printer","Mouse"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. A mobile phone can receive and play media content; the keyboard and mouse are input devices.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is NOT a characteristic of digital media?","options":["Create connections","Create community","Foster dynamic dialogue","Produce permanent records"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Digital media are dynamic and easily changed, connecting people and fostering dialogue rather than producing fixed permanent records.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is a pitfall of digital media?","options":["Boosting of brand","Encouraging too much follow up","Creating ethical issues in discovery","Stabilizing the value of resources"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Ethical problems such as privacy, piracy and misuse of discovered information are a downside of digital media; brand boosting is a benefit.","module":"1"},{"q":"The source of intellectual property can be traced to","options":["conferred authority","creation of the mind","inherited liability","shared effort"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Intellectual property refers to creations of the mind, such as inventions, designs and artistic works.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is MOST likely to raise ethical issues associated with digital media?","options":["Playing a rented DVD","Sharing a personal video production","Stripping of a DRM protected track","Downloading a Linux distribution movie using BitTorrent"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Removing DRM protection bypasses the copyright owner's controls, which raises ethical and legal issues.","module":"1"},{"q":"At which stage of the technology adoption life cycle are individuals more financially stable, have a higher social status and are well educated?","options":["Early adopters","Early innovators","Innovators","Early majority"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. In Rogers' adoption model, early adopters are typically well educated, financially secure and of higher social status, and are opinion leaders.","module":"1"},{"q":"The open movement does NOT include open","options":["standards","access movement","source movement","software initiative"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Open standards, open access and open source are parts of the open movement; 'open software initiative' is not a recognised part (it is the Open Source Initiative).","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is a multimedia software tool?","options":["Eclipse","Audacity","Microsoft Word","Google Chrome"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Audacity is an audio editing tool; Eclipse is a programming IDE, Word a word processor and Chrome a browser.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following are digital media platforms?<br>I. Satellite<br>II. Internet<br>III. 3D art","options":["I and II only","I and III only","II and III only","I, II and III"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Satellite and the Internet are platforms that deliver digital media; 3D art is a type of content, not a platform.","module":"1"},{"q":"A 'digital native' is an individual who","options":["uses technology without difficulty","repairs and maintains computers and servers","was born before the existence of digital technology","was born during the proliferation of digital technology"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. A digital native is someone born into the digital age, growing up with digital technology around them.","module":"2"},{"q":"A 'digital immigrant' is an individual who","options":["has adopted digital technology in later life","has moved away from digital technology","was born before the existence of digital technology","applies the principles of software development"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. A digital immigrant was born before the digital age and adopted digital technology later in life.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following BEST describes the 'digital media ecosystem' concept?","options":["An online library","A government information service","A business and corporate communications system","Media based on human communication, and shared electronically"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. The digital media ecosystem is the interconnected system of human communication that is created and shared electronically.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following channels of communication does NOT belong to the digital age?","options":["Fax","Blog","Wiki","Email"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Fax is an older, analogue-era technology; blogs, wikis and email are digital-age channels.","module":"2"},{"q":"Five persons are planning a presentation as a group project for a course, but are staying at different locations. They should use","options":["a wiki","a podcast","live streaming","a word processor"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. A wiki lets people in different locations collaboratively create and edit shared content.","module":"2"},{"q":"John has applied for a job at a digital media company. Which of the following does he need to demonstrate in order to be successful?","options":["Curiosity","Team spirit","Innovation","Research skills"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Digital media is a creative industry, so innovation is the key employability attribute employers seek.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is NOT an element of an elevator pitch?","options":["Concise","Complete","Catchy","Clear"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. An elevator pitch is brief, clear and catchy; it is not meant to be complete or exhaustive.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is NOT part of the digital media value chain?","options":["Single site service","Content creation","Content distribution","Customer management"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. The value chain covers creating, distributing and managing customers for content; 'single site service' is not a stage.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is a common work arrangement for digital media practitioners?","options":["Virtual team","Office team","Management team","Administrative team"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Digital media practitioners often work in virtual teams, collaborating online from different locations.","module":"2"},{"q":"Globalization is a process where an increased proportion of","options":["computer networking takes place","engagement takes place through social media","economic, social and cultural activities are carried out across national borders","economic, social and cultural activities are carried out within a country"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Globalization means more economic, social and cultural activity happens across national borders.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is a challenge in the digital media industry?","options":["Piracy","Convergence","Collaboration","Communication"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Piracy, the illegal copying and sharing of content, is a major challenge for the digital media industry.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is an example of debt funding?","options":["Loan","Crowd funding","Venture capital","Angel investment"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. A loan is debt funding because it must be repaid; venture capital and angel investment are equity funding.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following are major players in the digital media industry?","options":["Content producers","Information architects","Content strategists","Database administrators"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Content producers create the content at the core of the digital media industry.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following BEST describes the purpose of a project proposal?","options":["To provide the budget","To introduce the team","To provide project data","To introduce the project"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. A project proposal introduces and outlines the project to stakeholders; the budget and team are only parts of it.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following are key aspects of a project proposal?","options":["Conclusion, reference","Apps, disks, computers","Text messages, blogs, webpages","Overview, target audience, budget"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. A proposal typically includes a project overview, the target audience and the budget.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following sequences describes the creative process?<br>I. Develop<br>II. Implement<br>III. Create","options":["I, II, III","II, I, III","II, III, I","III, I, II"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Ideas are first created, then developed, and finally implemented.","module":"3"},{"q":"At which stage in the creative process would a person need to describe the issue to be solved?","options":["Ideation","Analysis","Acceptance","Implementation"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. During analysis the problem is examined and described before ideas are generated.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following is a tool for generating ideas?","options":["Texting","Mind mapping","Application development","PowerPoint presentation"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Mind-mapping visually links ideas, making it a useful idea-generation tool.","module":"3"},{"q":"What type of implementation of the creative process does the diagram illustrate?","passage":"<p>Item 34 refers to the following diagram.</p><p><i>Diagram:</i> seven arrow shapes in a single row, each pointing to the next, left to right: Accept Situation → Analyse → Define → Ideate → Select → Implement → Evaluate.</p>","options":["Cyclic","Linear","Feedback","Selection"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. The stages follow one after another in a straight line with no loop back, so the process is linear.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following activities is missing from the group shown below?<br><br>Creativity, innovation, concept development","options":["Ideation","Problem definition","Problem-solving","Brainstorming"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Creativity, innovation and concept development are all aspects of ideation, the idea-generating stage.","module":"3"},{"q":"A writer has developed an outline for a story and has decided to follow it through. What is the next stage in the creative process that should be undertaken?","options":["Ideation","Selection","Acceptance","Implementation"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. The idea has already been chosen, so the next stage is implementation, actually carrying it out.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following tasks must be completed prior to the actual making of a digital media product?","options":["Production","Fact finding","Preproduction","Problem-solving"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Pre-production (planning, scripting, storyboarding) must be finished before production begins.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following is a tool that can be used to edit photographs?","options":["Pixlr","Audacity","Movie Maker","Storyboard Pro"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Pixlr is an online photo editor; Audacity edits audio and MovieMaker edits video.","module":"3"},{"q":"Brainstorming, scriptwriting and storyboarding are part of","options":["ideation","production","pre-production","implementation"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Brainstorming, scripting and storyboarding are planning tasks carried out in pre-production.","module":"3"},{"q":"The diagram shown above is an illustration of","passage":"<p>Item 40 refers to the following diagram.</p><p><i>Diagram:</i> titled “Media Pre-Production Process”. A starburst labelled Brainstorm sits at the top. Below it four large downward arrows follow one another: Ideation → Writing → Pre-Visualization → Production Planning, ending in a box that reads: Script breakdown, Create shot list, Make shooting schedule, Make equipment lists. Bars down the sides label related tasks: Develop characters, settings, situations; Research; Develop themes/thesis; Storyboard; Scout locations; Assemble cast and crew.</p>","options":["ideation","scripting","production","preproduction"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. All of the steps shown are planning tasks done before shooting, which make up pre-production.","module":"3"},{"q":"How many sections are formed when imaginary lines are drawn in relation to the rule of thirds?","options":["Three","Six","Nine","Twelve"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Two horizontal and two vertical lines divide the frame into nine equal sections.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following groups consists of elements of composition?","options":["Video and lighting","Audio and composition","Rule of thirds and lighting","Rule of thirds and psychology of colours"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Rule of thirds and lighting are both elements used to compose an image or shot.","module":"3"},{"q":"A teacher would like her students to recap a particular lesson, ask questions, add comments, add discussion points and post any additional resources. Which digital media tool is most suitable to complete this task?","options":["A blog","Instant messaging","Audio recording","Video conferencing"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. A blog lets the teacher post a recap while students comment, ask questions and share resources in one place.","module":"3"},{"q":"The psychology of colours affects exactly how the consumer feels about and views content. Red is one of the primary psychological colors. Which of the following is NOT a positive effect of this colour?","options":["Strength","Warmth","Energy","Calmness"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Red is stimulating and associated with energy, warmth and strength; calmness is associated with blue.","module":"3"},{"q":"A couple is celebrating their fortieth wedding anniversary. Which of the following will BEST capture all aspects of the years they spent together?","options":["Photograph and video story","Video and audio story","Audio and photography story","Audio, photograph and video story"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Combining audio, photographs and video gives the richest multimedia record of their years together.","module":"3"}]},{"kind":"p1","id":"DP2014","title":"Paper 01 · 2014","time":90,"intro":"<p><b>CAPE Digital Media Unit 1 Paper 01 · 2014</b> · 1 hour 30 minutes · 45 items</p><ol><li>Answer <b>ALL</b> items. Each item has four options lettered (A), (B), (C), (D).</li><li>Start the optional timer to practise under exam conditions.</li><li>Submit to see your score, the key and an explanation for every item.</li></ol>","items":[{"q":"Which of the following is NOT a term used in digital media?","options":["Frame","JPEG","Isolation","Webcast"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Frame, JPEG and webcast are all common digital media terms; 'isolation' is not.","module":"1"},{"q":"In digital media, the acronym GIF stands for","options":["Graphical Innovation Font","Graphic Innovation Format","Graphic Interchange Format","Graphical Interchange Font"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. GIF stands for Graphics Interchange Format, an image file format.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following operating systems is open source?","options":["iOS","Android","Windows","Mac OS X"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Android is based on the open-source Linux kernel and released as the Android Open Source Project; the others are proprietary.","module":"1"},{"q":"The technology used by Betamax for saving is the","options":["Micro chip","Optical disc","Plastic disc","Magnetic tape"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Betamax was an analogue videocassette format that recorded on magnetic tape.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following BEST defines digital media?","options":["Text formatted for the Internet","Digitized content for use on laptops and tablets only","Digitized content that can be transmitted over the Internet or computer networks","Audio and video content that can be used on computer networks and other platforms"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Digital media is any digitized content (text, audio, video, graphics) that can be transmitted over the Internet or computer networks.","module":"1"},{"q":"The development of e-books using Caribbean examination papers and syllabus content is an example of using digital media to","options":["address local needs","eliminate the middleman","distribute content for free","bypass the publication industry"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Creating e-books from Caribbean exam and syllabus content serves the specific needs of local learners.","module":"1"},{"q":"A digital media platform is used for the delivery of","options":["open source software","multimedia files over an Intranet only","video, audio and/or data to multiple networks","streamed and downloadable music for online stores"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. A digital media platform delivers video, audio and data across multiple networks and devices.","module":"1"},{"q":"On a social networking site, Susan posted a video of herself dancing. Soon, persons started sharing the video link across the Internet. Which ethical issue is now of concern to Susan?","options":["Piracy","Privacy","Plagiarism","Creditability"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Her personal video is spreading beyond the audience she intended, which is a privacy concern.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following does a patent protect?","options":["An invention","A common logo","A borrowed idea","A political slogan"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Patents protect inventions; logos are protected by trademarks.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following does NOT present an ethical issue in the field of digital media?","options":["John sharing a video he shot and edited with his friends","John copying a commercial CD he borrowed from his friend","John selling a popular movie that he downloaded from YouTube","John downloading an expensive video editing suite from a file sharing site"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Sharing his own original video raises no ethical issue; the others involve copyright infringement or piracy.","module":"1"},{"q":"Jill is writing a new book and wants the final product to be in electronic format. Which of the following digital media businesses will be MOST suitable for doing this?","options":["Media houses","Effects factories","Interactive media firms","Advertising companies"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Interactive media firms produce digital and interactive products such as e-books.","module":"1"},{"q":"Your teacher has created a very interesting lesson plan and has decided she would like to share with other teachers by placing it on her blog. This lesson plan can be classified as","options":["an online educational resource","an open educational resource","a creative educational resource","a proprietary educational resource"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Teaching materials freely shared for others to use are open educational resources (OER).","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following tools is MOST appropriate for completing a wedding video?","options":["Picasa","Ardour","Moviemaker","Dreamweaver"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Movie Maker is a video editor; Picasa is for photos, Ardour for audio and Dreamweaver for websites.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following tools may be used in the preparation of a printable photo album?","options":["Picasa","Audacity","Animoto","Wavosaur"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Picasa organises and edits photos and can create printable collages and albums; Audacity and Wavosaur are audio editors.","module":"1"},{"q":"The phrase ‘pervasiveness of technology’ refers to","options":["the limited use of digital technology in some societies","the result of ‘throwing’ too much technology at a problem","the use of technology as a tool for misconduct in some societies","technology being widely available in almost every aspect of daily life"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Pervasive means spread throughout, so technology is present in almost every part of daily life.","module":"1"},{"q":"A digital native can be described as a person who","options":["uses the Internet to complete all tasks","uses all the social networks for communicating","has grown up using technology as a way of communicating with others","has adapted to the digital world using technology to communicate with others"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Digital natives grew up with digital technology; those who adapted later are digital immigrants.","module":"2"},{"q":"A person who is NOT part of the digital generation is MOST likely to","options":["pay bills in person","pay credit card bills online","purchase a tablet from e-bay","purchase a book online from Amazon"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Paying bills in person is a non-digital habit; the other options rely on online services.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following BEST describes the digital media environment?","options":["The availability of the Internet to do research","The use of mobile phones to complete daily tasks","The use of desktops and laptops to connect online and communicate","The proliferation of devices people use to consume content at home, at work and on the go"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. The digital media environment is the wide range of devices people use to consume content everywhere, not one device or task.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following devices is gaining prominence within the digital media ecosystem?","options":["PDA","Laptop","Mobile phone","Wearable computing"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Mobile phones were already established. Wearables such as smartwatches and fitness bands were the growing category.","module":"2"},{"q":"The stakeholder is MOST likely the","passage":"<p>This item refers to the following value chain.</p><p><i>Diagram:</i> five boxes joined by arrows, left to right: Content Creation → Aggregation &amp; Publishing → Distribution (Fixed &amp; Mobile) → Customer Environment → Stakeholder.</p>","options":["customer","programmer","content creator","content distributor"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. The chain flows from creation through distribution to the customer environment, so the end stakeholder who consumes the content is the customer.","module":"2"},{"q":"The owner of Jack’s Tyre Shop communicates with his suppliers in another territory using a computer with a microphone and a webcam connected to the Internet. Which of the following forms of communication uses ALL these technologies?","options":["Online chat","Telecommuting","Teleconferencing","Videoconferencing"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Videoconferencing uses a webcam, microphone and Internet connection for live audio and video meetings.","module":"2"},{"q":"A digitally connected team comprising members located in three different countries, completed a project. This model of working is known as","options":["internship","networking","telecommuting","microworking"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Telecommuting is working remotely through digital connections instead of being in a shared workplace.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is a MAJOR challenge faced by the digital media industry in the Caribbean landscape?","options":["Privacy","Storage","Reliable power supply","Availability of skilled workers"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. A shortage of skilled digital media workers is a key regional challenge to growing the industry.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is one of the MAJOR technical challenges that businesses may face in managing their digital media?","options":["Technical support","Backing up information","Finding information online","Managing employee records"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Digital media files are large and grow quickly, so backing them up reliably is a major technical challenge.","module":"2"},{"q":"John’s restaurant is located in a town that has a large population of digital immigrants. The manager notices that sales have dropped and is considering how to address this. Which of the following is the BEST method to advertise the restaurant’s goods to the community?","options":["Web signage","Text messages","E-mail messages","Internet promotions"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Digital immigrants are less at home online but commonly use basic mobile features, so text messages reach them most directly.","module":"2"},{"q":"Paul decides to open a business that designs websites; however, he needs to seek financing. He is required to provide a detailed business plan, along with any collateral, expected cash flow statement and asset liquidity position to the financial institution. What type of financing is Paul seeking?","options":["Debt","Equity","Grants","Company"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Asking for collateral and cash flow statements is typical of a bank loan, which is debt financing.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following may BEST enhance employability?","options":["Accounting practices","Building a presentation","Dressing appropriately","Developing a personal portfolio"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. A personal portfolio shows employers evidence of a digital media worker's skills and past work.","module":"2"},{"q":"The diagram can be used to complete a","passage":"<p>Item 28 refers to the following diagram.</p><p><i>Diagram:</i> four small cloud shapes down the left side. From each cloud, three arrows lead to three blank rectangular boxes on the right, making twelve empty boxes in all.</p>","options":["mind map","project pitch","project proposal","word association"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Each starting idea branches to several linked words, which is the pattern of a word association exercise. There is no single central topic, as a mind map would have.","module":"2"},{"q":"Concept formulation is important because it provides","options":["a set of materials to formulate and display ideas","an approach for forming relationships between concepts","a way to make connections and form relationships among peers","an opportunity to explore ideas by making connections between items of information"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Concept formulation lets you explore ideas by connecting pieces of information to build a concept.","module":"2"},{"q":"Oral presentation skills are important in the world of digital media because they<br>I. can help to communicate complex concepts<br>II. can enhance selling skills<br>III. allow for visual representation of data","options":["I only","I and II only","I and III only","I, II and III"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Good oral skills help explain complex ideas and sell or pitch them; visual representation of data comes from visual aids, not speaking.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following BEST describes the complete creative process?","options":["Designing a solution for two related problems","Taking a problem through to an implemented solution","Taking a problem through to a solution being designed","Taking a solution and retracing how the problem was solved"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. The complete creative process runs from accepting the problem all the way to implementing (and evaluating) the solution.","module":"3"},{"q":"During which stage of the creative process is the individual required to take time to study the problem at hand and how it relates to its various components?","options":["Analysis","Ideation","Implementation","Evaluation"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Analysis means studying the problem and how its parts relate.","module":"3"},{"q":"An entrepreneur is applying the creative process to solve a problem. At which point in the process will he do a mind mapping chart?","options":["Analysis","Selection","Ideation","Definition"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Mind mapping is an idea-generation technique, so it is used in the ideation stage.","module":"3"},{"q":"After studying and defining the problem, the next step in the creative process will be to","options":["sell ideas","generate ideas","evaluate ideas","accept ideas"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. After analysis and definition comes ideation, which is generating ideas.","module":"3"},{"q":"The diagram illustrates the stages in a creative process. The methodology illustrated in the diagram is","passage":"<p>Item 35 refers to the following diagram.</p><p><i>Diagram:</i> five circles joined by single lines in a zigzag chain, from bottom to top: Create the problem — Create the solution context — Create solutions — Develop details — Use and give feedback. There are no loops and no branches.</p>","options":["linear","cyclic","looped","branched"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. The stages follow one after another in a single line with no return path or branches, so the method is linear.","module":"3"},{"q":"A group, while working on a project, discusses the problem and records all ideas that come to mind. This is known as","options":["evaluating solutions","implementing solutions","brainstorming for solutions","communicating solutions"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Recording every idea that comes to mind without judging it is brainstorming.","module":"3"},{"q":"A software team is designing a website for a retail clothing store. Which of the following is an important factor when developing the site?","options":["PC compatibility","Mobile compatibility","Android compatibility","iPad compatibility"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Many shoppers browse on phones and tablets, so the site must work well on mobile devices generally, not just one platform.","module":"3"},{"q":"Pre-production relating to video refers to","options":["all tasks associated with the film","tasks that must be completed during filming","tasks that must be completed before filming","tasks that must be completed after filming"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Pre-production is all the planning done before filming starts, such as scripting, storyboarding and scheduling.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following is a core element in pre-production?","options":["Providing logistics for the crew","Ensuring that make-up is suitable","Scouting extensively for a location","Finding friendly resource personnel"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Location scouting is a core pre-production task done before shooting begins.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following should be considered when designing a website to assist toddlers in identifying different objects?","options":["Lighting","Bandwidth","Size of the logo","Psychology of colours"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Colour strongly affects young children's attention and recognition, so colour psychology is key for a toddler audience.","module":"3"},{"q":"Juanita has made a video of her baby brother, and would like to delete a part of the video that was included because she forgot to turn off the recording. Which of the following would be BEST for Juanita to use to accomplish this?","options":["Picasa","iMovie","Audacity","Wavepad"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. iMovie is a video editor that can trim unwanted footage; the other tools edit photos or audio.","module":"3"},{"q":"A client has asked you to ensure that an advertisement is seen mostly by persons between the ages of 19 and 21. What type of targeting would need to be used?","options":["Contextual","Behavioural","Geographic","Demographic"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Targeting by age is demographic targeting.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following can be used for organizing information between groups of people?","options":["Blog","Wiki","Podcast","Live streaming"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. A wiki lets many users work together to add, edit and organise shared information.","module":"3"},{"q":"Julie started an assignment in the computer lab at school with the intention of continuing at home. Although she did not have her flash drive, she was still able to access the document at home. Which of the following did Julie MOST likely use to save her document?","options":["Hardware","Mobile app","Web browser","Cloud storage"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Cloud storage keeps files online so they can be opened from any connected device.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following formats is BEST for creating a video of a school’s graduation ceremony?","options":[".mpeg2",".jpeg",".wav",".gif"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. MPEG-2 is a video format; JPEG and GIF are image formats and WAV is audio.","module":"3"}]},{"kind":"p1","id":"DP2015","title":"Paper 01 · 2015","time":90,"intro":"<p><b>CAPE Digital Media Unit 1 Paper 01 · 2015</b> · 1 hour 30 minutes · 45 items</p><ol><li>Answer <b>ALL</b> items. Each item has four options lettered (A), (B), (C), (D).</li><li>Start the optional timer to practise under exam conditions.</li><li>Submit to see your score, the key and an explanation for every item.</li></ol>","items":[{"q":"Software that can be used and modified from its original source and sold to other users is BEST described as open","options":["data","source","domain","educational resources"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Open source software has source code that anyone may use, modify and redistribute, including selling it.","module":"1"},{"q":"In digital media, the acronym GIF stands for","options":["Graphical Innovation Font","Graphic Innovation Format","Graphical Interchange Font","Graphics Interchange Format"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. GIF stands for Graphics Interchange Format, an image file format.","module":"1"},{"q":"John wants to reduce the size of his audio file before putting it on his website. Which of the following is MOST useful for John’s situation?","options":["Bandwidth","Transcoding","Compression","Decompression"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Compression makes a file smaller so it loads and streams faster on the web.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following icons represents the Creative Commons licensing system?","options":["[Icon: a person figure in a circle]","[Icon: a crossed-out dollar sign in a circle]","[Icon: a circular arrow in a circle]","[Icon: the letters 'cc' in a circle]"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. The 'cc' in a circle is the main Creative Commons logo; the other icons stand for individual licence conditions (Attribution, NonCommercial, ShareAlike).","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following BEST defines digital media?","options":["Text formatted for the Internet","Digitized content for use on laptops and tablets only","Audio and video content that can be used on computer networks and other platforms","Digitized content that can be transmitted over the Internet or computer networks"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Digital media is any digitized content (text, audio, video, graphics) that can be transmitted over the Internet or computer networks.","module":"1"},{"q":"The development of e-books using Caribbean examination papers and syllabus content is an example of using digital media to","options":["address local needs","eliminate the middleman","distribute content for free","bypass the publication industry"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Creating e-books from Caribbean exam and syllabus content serves the specific needs of local learners.","module":"1"},{"q":"A digital media platform is used for the delivery of","options":["open source software","multimedia files over an Intranet only","video, audio and/or data to multiple networks","streamed and downloadable music for online stores"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. A digital media platform delivers video, audio and data across multiple networks and devices.","module":"1"},{"q":"On a social networking site, Susan posted a video of herself dancing. Soon, persons started sharing the video link across the Internet. Which of the following ethical issues should be of concern to Susan?","options":["Piracy","Privacy","Plagiarism","Creditability"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Her personal video is spreading beyond the audience she intended, which is a privacy concern.","module":"1"},{"q":"A patent is a set of exclusive rights that protects","options":["an idea","an invention","a common logo","a political slogan"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Patents protect inventions, not bare ideas; logos are protected by trademarks.","module":"1"},{"q":"Arrange the items below to represent the CORRECT sequence of creating a digital video.<br>I. Editing<br>II. Production<br>III. Storyboarding","options":["I, II, III","I, III, II","II, III, I","III, II, I"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Storyboarding is pre-production, then the footage is shot (production), then it is edited (post-production).","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following tools is associated with photo editing?","options":["YouTube","Audacity","Live Quartz","Aptana Studio"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. LiveQuartz is an image and photo editor; YouTube is video sharing, Audacity edits audio and Aptana Studio is a web IDE.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following activities could be considered a cybercrime?","options":["Unlocking a mobile phone","Intercepting mobile communication","Saving customer data to a thumb drive","Using a free software to develop an app"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Intercepting other people's communications without authorisation is illegal interception, a cybercrime.","module":"1"},{"q":"Spencer downloaded the latest calypso music and ‘burnt’ copies of CDs to sell to his friends. What ethical issue would his action raise?","options":["Plagiarism","Identity theft","Internet fraud","Copyright infringement"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Copying and selling music without the rights holder's permission is copyright infringement (piracy).","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following does NOT present an ethical issue in the field of digital media?","options":["John sharing a video he shot and edited with his friends","John copying a commercial CD he borrowed from his friend","John selling a popular movie that he downloaded from YouTube","John downloading an expensive video editing suite from a file sharing site"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Sharing his own original video raises no ethical issue; the others involve copyright infringement or piracy.","module":"1"},{"q":"The phrase ‘pervasiveness of technology’ refers to the","options":["limited use of digital technology in some societies","result of ‘throwing’ too much technology at a problem","use of technology as a tool for misconduct in some societies","availability of technology in almost every aspect of daily life"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Pervasive means spread throughout, so technology is present in almost every part of daily life.","module":"1"},{"q":"A digital native can be described as a person who","options":["uses the Internet to complete all tasks","uses all the social networks for communicating","has grown up using technology as a way of communicating with others","has adapted to the digital world using technology to communicate with others"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Digital natives grew up with digital technology; those who adapted later are digital immigrants.","module":"2"},{"q":"Using the following list of elements, what is the MOST likely common sequence for pitching a project?<br>I. Proposal<br>II. Problem<br>III. Conclusion","options":["I, II, III","II, III, I","II, I, III","III, II, I"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. A pitch first states the problem, then proposes the solution, then concludes.","module":"2"},{"q":"After brainstorming and having identified her target audience, Anika combined various media elements to create a layout for her new website. Which of the following BEST describes the phase she has just completed?","options":["Planning","Distributing","Wire framing","Interface design"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Combining actual media elements into a page layout is interface design; a wireframe is only a bare skeleton without media.","module":"2"},{"q":"Richard is making a presentation to young adults on the topic of ‘Digital media’. Which of the following visual aids is LEAST likely to be suitable for this presentation?","options":["Video","Animation","Wireframe","Interactive slide show"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. A wireframe is a bare planning sketch, not an engaging visual aid; video, animation and interactive slides suit a young audience.","module":"2"},{"q":"The stakeholder is MOST likely the","passage":"<p>This item refers to the following value chain.</p><p><i>Diagram:</i> five boxes joined by arrows, left to right: Content Creation → Aggregation &amp; Publishing → Distribution (Fixed &amp; Mobile) → Customer Environment → Stakeholder.</p>","options":["customer","programmer","content creator","content distributor"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. The chain flows from creation through distribution to the customer environment, so the end stakeholder who consumes the content is the customer.","module":"2"},{"q":"The digital media ecosystem can BEST be described as the","options":["environment in which digital media exists","IT industry and the persons that support digital media","components of digital media working together continuously","components of digital media and the infrastructure that supports it"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. The ecosystem includes both the parts of digital media (content, devices, users) and the infrastructure that supports them.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following terms BEST describes the emergence of worldwide markets?","options":["E-commerce","Globalization","Internationalization","Geographical information"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Globalization is the integration of national economies into worldwide markets.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is a MAJOR challenge faced by the digital media industry in the Caribbean landscape?","options":["Privacy","Storage","Reliable power supply","Availability of skilled workers"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. A shortage of skilled digital media workers is a key regional challenge to growing the industry.","module":"2"},{"q":"John wants to seek funding for his business proposal but the banking sector does not want to take the risks to provide funding. Which of the following is the BEST source of funding for his business proposal?","options":["Donations","Credit union","Crowd funding","Private investors"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Crowdfunding raises small amounts from many people online, which avoids relying on risk-averse lenders.","module":"2"},{"q":"The Digital Media Value Chain describes","options":["an enhancement","a creative process","a planning process","an implementation"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. A value chain shows how value is added (enhanced) at each stage as content moves from creation to the customer.","module":"2"},{"q":"Paul decides to open a business that designs websites; however, he needs to seek financing. He is required to provide a detailed business plan, along with collateral, expected cash flow statement and asset liquidity position to the financial institution. What type of financing is Paul seeking?","options":["Debt","Equity","Grant","Company"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Asking for collateral and cash flow statements is typical of a bank loan, which is debt financing.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following activities BEST describes the process of brainstorming?","options":["Defining the problem","Documenting the design process","Testing the effectiveness of a prototype","Drawing a diagram to represent ideas linked to a central keyword"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Brainstorming generates and links many ideas around a central topic, often drawn as a diagram. The other options belong to other stages.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is NOT a method of idea generation?","options":["Free writing","Brainstorming","Digital mapping","Word association"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Free writing, brainstorming and word association are standard idea-generation techniques; 'digital mapping' is not (mind mapping is).","module":"2"},{"q":"Concept formulation is important because it provides","options":["a set of materials to prepare and display ideas","an approach for forming relationships between concepts","a way to make connections and form relationships among peers","an opportunity to explore ideas by making connections between items of information"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Concept formulation lets you explore ideas by connecting pieces of information to build a concept.","module":"2"},{"q":"Oral presentation skills are important in the world of digital media because they<br>I. can enhance marketing skills<br>II. allow for visual representation of data<br>III. can help to communicate complex concepts","options":["I only","I and II only","I and III only","I, II and III"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Good oral skills help market ideas and explain complex concepts; visual representation of data comes from visual aids, not speaking.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following BEST describes the complete creative process?","options":["Designing a solution for two related problems","Taking a problem through to an implemented solution","Taking a problem through to a solution being designed","Taking a solution and retracing how the problem was solved"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. The complete creative process runs from accepting the problem all the way to implementing (and evaluating) the solution.","module":"3"},{"q":"During which stage of the creative process is the individual required to take time to study the problem at hand and how it relates to its various components?","options":["Analysis","Ideation","Evaluation","Implementation"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Analysis means studying the problem and how its parts relate.","module":"3"},{"q":"An entrepreneur is applying the creative process to solve a problem. At which point in the process should he do a mind-mapping chart?","options":["Ideation","Selection","Analysis","Definition"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Mind mapping is an idea-generation technique, so it is used in the ideation stage.","module":"3"},{"q":"After studying and defining the problem, the next step in the creative process is to","options":["sell ideas","generate ideas","evaluate ideas","accept ideas"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. After analysis and definition comes ideation, which is generating ideas.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following terms BEST describes this approach?","passage":"<p>This item refers to the following diagram which shows an approach to the creative process.</p><p><i>Diagram:</i> from <b>Accept situation</b> two arrows lead off. The upper path goes to Analysis, which splits into Ideate and Define. The lower path goes to Define, which splits into Ideate and Re-Analyze; Re-Analyze leads to another Ideate. Every one of these paths ends at <b>Select</b>. Select leads to Implement, which splits into Evaluate and Re-Analyze, and Re-Analyze also points to Evaluate.</p>","options":["Linear","Cyclic","Feedback","Branched"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. The process splits into several alternative paths that later rejoin, so it is a branched approach.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following is NOT a core preproduction task when doing digital video production?","options":["Logistics","Budgeting","Visual Effects","Storyboarding"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Visual effects are added in post-production; logistics, budgeting and storyboarding are done before filming.","module":"3"},{"q":"A software team is designing a website for a retail clothing store. Which of the following is an important factor to be considered?","options":["PC compatibility","iPad compatibility","Mobile compatibility","Android compatibility"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Many shoppers browse on phones and tablets, so the site must work well on mobile devices generally, not just one platform.","module":"3"},{"q":"The arrangement of elements within a user interface or layout is called","options":["use of space","composition","rule of thirds","visual hierarchy"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Composition is the overall arrangement of visual elements in a layout.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following is NOT considered part of the five-step approach to the ideation process in developing an inventive solution?","options":["Define","Validate","Generate","Evaluate"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Defining the problem, generating ideas and evaluating them are core ideation steps; validation is not part of this model.","module":"3"},{"q":"During which of the following phases of producing a gaming website would JavaScript be added?","options":["Creating","Planning","Ideation","Implementation"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Code such as JavaScript is written and added when the planned design is built, which is the implementation phase.","module":"3"},{"q":"Sunil is editing a video, the final output will be posted on the Internet. Which of the following formats would BEST allow for immediate use on the web?","options":["FLV","AVI","MOV","MPEG-4"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. FLV (Flash Video) was designed for streaming video on the web. MPEG-4 is also widely used online, which makes this item debatable.","module":"3"},{"q":"What type of targeting should be used to ensure that an advertisement is seen mostly by persons between the ages of 19 and 21?","options":["Contextual","Behavioural","Geographic","Demographic"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Targeting by age is demographic targeting.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following can be used for organizing information between groups of people?","options":["Blog","Wiki","Podcast","Live streaming"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. A wiki lets many users work together to add, edit and organise shared information.","module":"3"},{"q":"A video was edited using a video editing suite. In which of the following ways may it be shared?<br>I. Exported as an FLV file<br>II. Exported as a WAV file<br>III. Uploaded online to YouTube","options":["I and II only","I and III only","II and III only","I, II and III"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. FLV is a video format and YouTube hosts video; WAV is audio only and cannot hold the video.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following formats is BEST for creating a video of a school’s graduation ceremony?","options":[".mpeg2",".jpeg",".wav",".gif"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. MPEG-2 is a video format; JPEG and GIF are image formats and WAV is audio.","module":"3"}]},{"kind":"p1","id":"DP2016","title":"Paper 01 · 2016","time":90,"intro":"<p><b>CAPE Digital Media Unit 1 Paper 01 · 2016</b> · 1 hour 30 minutes · 45 items</p><p class=\"hint\">Original: a retyped copy of the 2016 paper; its items are not grouped by module.</p><ol><li>Answer <b>ALL</b> items. Each item has four options lettered (A), (B), (C), (D).</li><li>Start the optional timer to practise under exam conditions.</li><li>Submit to see your score, the key and an explanation for every item.</li></ol>","items":[{"q":"Which of the following gives the correct sequence for pitching a project?<br>I. Proposal<br>II. Problem<br>III. Conclusion","options":["I, II, III","II, III, I","II, I, III","III, II, I"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. A pitch first states the problem, then presents the proposed solution, and ends with a conclusion.","module":"2"},{"q":"The term 'new media' refers to the use of technologies to","options":["Store data securely","Communicate with an audience","Provide content to mobile devices","Ensure that content is up to date"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. New media describes digital, often interactive, technologies used to communicate content to an audience.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is NOT considered a form of digital communication?","options":["Fax","Skype","E-mail","Mobile phone"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Traditional fax transmits scanned documents as analogue signals over telephone lines, unlike Skype, e-mail and mobile phones.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following does NOT present an ethical issue in the field of digital media?","options":["John sharing a video he shot and edited with his friends","Camille copying a commercial CD she borrowed from her friend","Simone selling a popular movie that she downloaded from YouTube","Rayman downloading an expensive video editing suite from a file sharing site"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. John owns the video he created, so sharing it raises no copyright or ethical problem; the others involve copying or distributing others' work.","module":"1"},{"q":"Michael has developed a mobile app that allows users to enter their gender and shoe size; it then searches for appropriate shoes at two major online retailers.<br>Which of the following would NOT have been a necessary step in the process of developing this mobile app?","options":["Developing a story board and a shot list","Obtaining a price list from a local shoe retailer","Doing a survey to determine the appropriateness of the app","Obtaining a list of all the possible shoe sizes from a local shoe retailer"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. The app only searches two online retailers, so a local retailer’s price list plays no part in developing it.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following BEST describes the complete creative process?","options":["Designing a solution for two related problems","Taking a problem through to an implemented solution","Taking a problem through to a solution being designed","Designing a solution and testing how the problem is to be solved"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. The full creative process runs from accepting and defining a problem all the way to implementing (and evaluating) a solution.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following is NOT a skill needed to enhance entrepreneurship in the digital media industry?","options":["Programming skill","Continuous learning","Portfolio development","Ability to market ideas"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Entrepreneurship depends on learning, a portfolio and marketing ideas; programming is a technical skill, not an entrepreneurial one.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is likely to occur MORE frequently given the increased use of the Internet and digital tools?","options":["Material discoveries","Dynamic discussions","Raising social issues","Raising ethical issues"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Wider use of the Internet and digital tools brings more ethical questions such as privacy, piracy and plagiarism.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is necessary in clearly defining a problem?","options":["Accumulate information","Decompose the problem","Provide opportunities for expansion","Utilize convergent and divergent thinking"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Breaking a problem into its parts clarifies exactly what must be solved, which is the purpose of the define stage.","module":"3"},{"q":"A production team is considering using existing material such as photographs, audio and graphics sourced from the Internet. Which of the following intellectual property issues should the team be concerned with?","options":["Libel","Slander","Copyright","Trademark"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Photographs, audio and graphics are creative works protected by copyright, so permission or licensing is needed.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following statements are TRUE about venture capitalists?<br>I. They only fund large business<br>II. They provide equity for businesses<br>III. They expect high returns on their investments","options":["I and II only","I and III only","II and III only","I, II and III"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Venture capitalists invest equity, often in small high-growth start-ups, and expect high returns for the risk they take.","module":"2"},{"q":"When measuring environmental challenges and opportunities, context is usually measured as","options":["Local and global","Outer and inner","Personal and public","Individual and mutual"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Environmental scanning considers the context at local and global levels.","module":"2"},{"q":"Camille was born in 2013 and is referred to as a digital native because","options":["Persons born after the year 2000 all have digital birth certificates","Her parents are likely young enough to have grown up in the digital age","Being born after the year 2010, her medical records are digitally managed","She was born during or after the general introduction of digital technology"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. A digital native is someone who grew up during or after the widespread introduction of digital technology.","module":"2"},{"q":"Anila is designing an interactive map for her school’s website and wants to highlight multiple locations on the map. Which of the following software would be BEST for implementing the map?","options":["Photo editing","Movie editing","Mind mapping","Online mapping"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Online mapping tools such as Google My Maps let you mark multiple locations on an interactive map for a website.","module":"3"},{"q":"A digital media platform is a digitized platform used for","options":["Recycling audio, video and data","Sharing data openly among students and teachers","Storing different types of data within a closed network","Delivering audio, video and data across multiple networks"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Digital media platforms exist to deliver audio, video and data to users across multiple networks.","module":"1"},{"q":"James printed a copy of his friend's school-based assessment and submitted it to his teacher as his own. Which of the following ethical issues would arise from his action?","options":["Libel","Hacking","Plagiarism","Copyright infringement"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Presenting someone else's work as your own is plagiarism.","module":"1"},{"q":"Michael has developed a mobile app that allows users to enter their gender and shoe size; it then searches for appropriate shoes at two major online retailers.<br>Which of the following would have been the MOST important consideration when designing this mobile app?","options":["Making the size of the app as big as possible","Including an icon for different types of phones","Including a tool that detects geographical location","Ensuring that it works with different screen sizes"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Mobile apps run on many devices, so responsive design for different screen sizes is the key consideration.","module":"3"},{"q":"Software that can be used and modified from its original source and sold to other users is BEST described as open","options":["data","source","domain","educational resources"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Open source software has source code that anyone may use, modify and redistribute, including selling it.","module":"1"},{"q":"An effects factory will MOST likely work on<br>I. Mobile apps<br>II. Digital video<br>III. Digital audio","options":["I only","II only","III only","I, II and III"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. An effects factory (visual effects studio) mainly produces visual effects for film and digital video.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is NOT considered part of the five-step approach to the ideation process in developing an inventive solution?","options":["Define","Validate","Generate","Evaluate"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Defining the problem, generating ideas and evaluating them are core ideation steps; validation is not part of this model.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following terms BEST describes the approach to the creative process shown in the diagram above?","passage":"<p>Item 21 refers to the following diagram.</p><p><i>Diagram:</i> from <b>Accept situation</b> two arrows lead off. The upper path goes to Analysis, which splits into Ideate and Define. The lower path goes to Define, which splits into Ideate and Re-Analyze; Re-Analyze leads to another Ideate. Every one of these paths ends at <b>Select</b>. Select leads to Implement, which splits into Evaluate and Re-Analyze, and Re-Analyze also points to Evaluate.</p>","options":["Linear","Cyclic","Feedback","Branched"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. The process splits into alternative paths that later rejoin, which is a branched approach.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following stages requires understanding of the problem in the Universal Traveler model of the creative process?","options":["Ideation","Analysis","Acceptance","Implementation"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. In the Universal Traveler model, the Analysis stage gathers facts to understand the problem.","module":"3"},{"q":"The stakeholder, in the diagram above, is MOST likely the","passage":"<p>Item 23 refers to the following value chain.</p><p><i>Diagram:</i> five boxes joined by arrows, left to right: Content Creation → Aggregation &amp; Publishing → Distribution (Fixed &amp; Mobile) → Customer Environment → Stakeholder.</p>","options":["Customer","Programmer","Content creator","Content distributor"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. The chain ends with content reaching the customer's environment, so the final stakeholder is the customer who consumes the content.","module":"2"},{"q":"Storyboard Pro, Animoto and Wavepad are all","options":["Audio players","Digital media tools","Video editing software","Photo editing software"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. They cover storyboarding, video creation and audio editing, so the only common category is digital media tools.","module":"3"},{"q":"A software team is designing a website for a retail clothing store. Which of the following is an important factor to be considered?","options":["PC compatibility","iPad compatibility","Mobile compatibility","Android compatibility"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Many shoppers browse on phones and tablets, so the site must work well on mobile devices generally, not just one platform.","module":"3"},{"q":"Historically Web 2.0 tends to refer to a time in the history of the Internet when","options":["Web 1.0 websites started to become less popular","Websites began to adopt HTML5 and Javascript","The option for users to add or modify information became more prevalent","A new version of the web was released by the World Wide Web Consortium"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Web 2.0 describes the shift to user-generated content and interaction, such as blogs, wikis and social media.","module":"1"},{"q":"A patent is a set of exclusive rights that protects","options":["An idea","An invention","A common logo","A political slogan"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. A patent grants exclusive rights over an invention; ideas alone cannot be patented and logos are protected by trademarks.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following working models is also referred to as 'nomadic' working?","options":["Teleworking","Microworking","Virtual working","Regular working"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Nomadic or virtual working means working from any location using mobile technology, not tied to a fixed office.","module":"2"},{"q":"The term 'bandwidth' refers to","options":["A high-speed internet connection","The download speed of a connection","The number of IP addresses present in a network","The transmission capacity of a communication line"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Bandwidth is the maximum data transmission capacity of a communication channel.","module":"1"},{"q":"The process of idea generation encourages","options":["Criticism","Limited ideas","Outlandish ideas","The discarding of ideas"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Idea generation (brainstorming) defers judgement and encourages wild, outlandish ideas to maximise options.","module":"3"},{"q":"Concept formulation is important because it provides","options":["a set of materials to prepare and display ideas","an approach for forming relationships between concepts","a way to make connections and form relationships among peers","an opportunity to explore ideas by making connections between items of information"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Concept formulation lets you explore ideas by connecting pieces of information into a coherent concept.","module":"3"},{"q":"A collection of systems that is used to protect the copyright of electronic media is referred to as a","options":["Copyright system","Digital rights system","Digital rights management system","Copyright rights management system"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Digital Rights Management (DRM) systems control access to and copying of copyrighted digital media.","module":"1"},{"q":"Paul decides to open a business that designs websites; however, he needs to seek financing. He is required to provide a detailed business plan, along with collateral, expected cash flow statement and asset liquidity position to the financial institution. What type of financing is Paul seeking?","options":["Debt","Equity","Grant","Company"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Lenders ask for collateral and cash-flow evidence because a loan is debt financing that must be repaid.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following activities can be considered a cybercrime?","options":["Unlocking a mobile phone","Intercepting mobile communication","Saving customer data to a thumb drive","Using a free software to develop an app"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Intercepting other people's communications without authorisation is an illegal computer-related crime.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is an important part of the planning process when preparing to build a website?","options":["Wireframe","Logo design","Dreamweaver","Colour scheme"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. A wireframe maps out the page layout and structure during website planning, before design and building.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following represents a step in the creation stage of a website?","options":["Exporting","Adding content","Creating a site map","Determining distribution methods"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Adding content is done while building the site; a site map is planned earlier, and exporting and distribution come later.","module":"3"},{"q":"Audio editing can be done using","options":["GIMP","iTunes","Animoto","GoldWave"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. GoldWave is an audio editor; GIMP edits images, iTunes plays media and Animoto makes videos.","module":"3"},{"q":"The digital media ecosystem can BEST be described as the","options":["Environment in which digital media exists","IT industry and the persons who support digital media","Components of digital media working together continuously","Components of digital media and the infrastructure that supports them"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. The digital media ecosystem includes the content and components of digital media together with the infrastructure that supports and delivers them.","module":"2"},{"q":"Susan posted a video of herself dancing on a social networking site. Immediately after, persons started sharing the video link across the Internet.<br>Which of the following ethical issues should Susan have considered before posting?","options":["Piracy","Privacy","Plagiarism","Creditability"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Once posted, personal content can spread beyond her control, so she should have considered her privacy.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is considered a MAJOR benefit of telecommuting?","options":["Reduced stress levels","Controlled environment","Decreased wastage of time","Reduced travel cost and time"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Working from home removes the daily commute, saving travel cost and time.","module":"2"},{"q":"What type of targeting should be used to ensure that an advertisement is seen mostly by persons between the ages of 19 and 21?","options":["Contextual","Behavioural","Geographic","Demographic"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Targeting by age is demographic targeting.","module":"1"},{"q":"Omar wants to seek funding for his business proposal. The banking sector does not want to take the risk of providing funding. What is the BEST alternative source of funding for his business proposal?","options":["Savings","Credit union","Crowdfunding","Stock market"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Crowdfunding raises money from many people online without needing a lender to accept the risk.","module":"2"},{"q":"A storyboard is created","options":["Before shooting a movie","Whenever the author wants it","After shooting animated feature","Immediately after a screenplay is written"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. A storyboard is a pre-production tool used to plan shots before filming begins.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following are components of a project proposal?<br>I. Objectives<br>II. Project duration<br>III. Expected results","options":["I and II only","I and III only","II and III only","I, II and III"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. A project proposal states its objectives, timeline and expected outcomes.","module":"2"},{"q":"Technological advances in digital media have brought opportunities as well as challenges in the delivery of innovative content experiences. These challenges may include the<br>I. Increasing cost of maintaining the latest technology<br>II. Complexity of continually adapting to the latest technology<br>III. Difficulty of disposing of old technology","options":["I only","I and II only","II and III only","I, II and III"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Keeping up with technology raises costs, demands constant adaptation and creates e-waste, so all three are challenges.","module":"2"}]},{"kind":"p1","id":"DP2017","title":"Paper 01 · 2017","time":90,"intro":"<p><b>CAPE Digital Media Unit 1 Paper 01 · 2017</b> · 1 hour 30 minutes · 45 items</p><ol><li>Answer <b>ALL</b> items. Each item has four options lettered (A), (B), (C), (D).</li><li>Start the optional timer to practise under exam conditions.</li><li>Submit to see your score, the key and an explanation for every item.</li></ol>","items":[{"q":"Software that can be used and modified from its original source and sold to other users is BEST described as open","options":["data","source","domain","educational resources"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Open source software has source code that anyone may use, modify and redistribute, including selling it.","module":"1"},{"q":"Historically, Web 2.0 tends to refer to a time in the history of the Internet when","options":["Web 1.0 websites started to become less popular","websites began to adopt HTML5 and JavaScript","a new version of the web was released by the World Wide Web consortium","interaction and ability for users to add or modify information became more important"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Web 2.0 describes the shift to a participatory web where users create, share and modify content; it was not a formal release by the W3C.","module":"1"},{"q":"John wants to reduce the size of his audio file before putting it on his website. Which of the following would be MOST useful in reducing the size of the file?","options":["Bandwidth","Transcoding","Compression","Decompression"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Compression removes redundant or less important data so the file takes up less storage space.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is an open source operating system?","options":["iOS","Android","Windows","Mac OS X"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Android is built on the open source Android Open Source Project and Linux kernel; the others are proprietary.","module":"1"},{"q":"A digital media platform is a digitized platform used for","options":["recycling audio, video and data","sharing data openly among students and teachers","storing different types of data within a closed network","delivering audio, video and data across multiple networks"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Digital media platforms exist to deliver audio, video and data to users across multiple networks.","module":"1"},{"q":"A collection of systems used to protect the copyrights of electronic media is referred to as","options":["copyright system","digital rights system","digital rights management","copyright rights management"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Digital rights management (DRM) is the set of technologies used to control access to and copying of copyrighted digital content.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following types of licenses allows an author to give people the right to use, share and build upon his work?","options":["Patent","Copyright","Trademark","Creative Commons"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Creative Commons licences let creators grant the public permission to use, share and build on their work under stated conditions.","module":"1"},{"q":"On a social networking site, Susan posted a video of herself dancing. Soon, persons started sharing the video link across the Internet. Which of the following ethical issues should be of concern to Susan?","options":["Piracy","Privacy","Plagiarism","Creditability"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Her personal video is spreading beyond the audience she intended, which is a privacy concern.","module":"1"},{"q":"A patent is a set of exclusive rights that protects","options":["an idea","an invention","a common logo","a political slogan"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Patents protect inventions, not bare ideas; logos are protected by trademarks.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following does NOT present an ethical issue in the field of digital media?","options":["John sharing a video he shot and edited with his friends","John copying a commercial CD he borrowed from his friend","John selling a popular movie that he downloaded from YouTube","John downloading an expensive video editing suite from a file sharing site"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Sharing his own original video raises no ethical issue; the others involve copyright infringement or piracy.","module":"1"},{"q":"The term 'bandwidth' refers to","options":["a high-speed Internet connection","the download speed of a connection","the number of IP addresses present in a network","the transmission capacity of a communication line"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Bandwidth is the maximum data transmission capacity of a communication channel.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following activities could be considered a cybercrime?","options":["Unlocking a mobile phone","Intercepting mobile communication","Saving customer data to a thumb drive","Using a free software to develop an app"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Intercepting other people's communications without authorisation is illegal interception, a cybercrime.","module":"1"},{"q":"Audio editing can be done using","options":["GIMP","iTunes","Animoto","GoldWave"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. GoldWave is an audio editor; GIMP edits images, iTunes plays media and Animoto makes videos.","module":"1"},{"q":"The development of e-books using Caribbean Examinations Council papers and syllabus content is an example of using digital media to","options":["address local needs","eliminate the middleman","distribute content for free","bypass the publication industry"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. E-books built from CXC syllabus content serve the specific needs of Caribbean students, which is addressing local needs.","module":"1"},{"q":"The phrase ‘pervasiveness of technology’ refers to the","options":["limited use of digital technology in some societies","result of ‘throwing’ too much technology at a problem","availability of technology in almost every aspect of daily life","use of technology as a tool for misconduct in some societies"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Pervasive means spread throughout, so technology is present in almost every part of daily life.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following skills may NOT be needed to enhance entrepreneurship in the digital media industry?","options":["Programming","Continuous learning","Portfolio development","Ability to market ideas"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Continuous learning, a portfolio and marketing ability are core entrepreneurial skills, while programming is a technical skill not every digital media entrepreneur needs.","module":"2"},{"q":"Steven wants to start a music production business that requires $100 000 to start up. He has $50 000 in savings and his brother invests $25 000. He then acquires a $25 000 loan from the bank to make up the total amount.<br>This type of funding can be BEST described as","options":["debt","equity","debt and equity","venture capital"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. The savings and his brother's investment are equity, while the bank loan is debt, so the funding is a mix of both.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is considered a MAJOR benefit of telecommuting?","options":["Reduced stress levels","Controlled environment","Decreased wastage of time","Reduced travel cost"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Working from home removes the daily commute, so the most direct benefit is reduced travel cost.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following statements are TRUE about venture capitalists?<br>I. They only fund large businesses.<br>II. They provide equity for businesses.<br>III. They expect high returns on their investments.","options":["I and II only","I and III only","II and III only","I, II and III"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Venture capitalists invest money in exchange for equity and expect high returns; they often fund small, high-growth start-ups rather than only large businesses.","module":"2"},{"q":"The stakeholder is MOST likely the","passage":"<p>This item refers to the following value chain.</p><p><i>Diagram:</i> five boxes joined by arrows, left to right: Content Creation → Aggregation &amp; Publishing → Distribution (Fixed &amp; Mobile) → Customer Environment → Stakeholder.</p>","options":["customer","programmer","content creator","content distributor"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. The stakeholder sits at the end of the chain after the customer environment, so it is the customer who consumes the content.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following are the parts of a project proposal?<br>I. Objectives<br>II. Project duration<br>III. Expected results","options":["I and II only","I and III only","II and III only","I, II and III"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. A project proposal sets out its objectives, the timeline or duration, and the expected results or outcomes.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following terms BEST describes the emergence of worldwide markets?","options":["E-commerce","Globalization","Internationalization","Geographical information"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Globalization is the integration of national economies into worldwide markets.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is a MAJOR challenge faced by the digital media industry in the Caribbean?","options":["Privacy","Storage","Reliable power supply","Availability of skilled workers"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. The Caribbean digital media industry is limited by a shortage of trained, skilled practitioners.","module":"2"},{"q":"John wants to seek funding for his business proposal but the banking sector does not want to take the risks to provide funding. Which of the following is the BEST source of funding for his business proposal?","options":["Donation","Credit union","Crowdfunding","Private investor"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Crowdfunding raises small amounts from many people online, so it does not depend on a lender or single investor accepting the risk.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following may BEST enhance employability?","options":["Accounting practices","Building a presentation","Dressing appropriately","Developing a personal portfolio"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. A personal portfolio shows employers evidence of a digital media worker's skills and past work.","module":"2"},{"q":"Paul decides to open a business that designs websites; however, he needs to seek financing. The financial institution requires him to provide a detailed business plan, an expected cash flow statement, an asset liquidity position, and collateral. What type of financing is Paul seeking?","options":["Debt","Equity","Grant","Company"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Collateral and cash-flow evidence are required when borrowing a loan, which is debt financing.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following activities BEST describes the process of brainstorming?","options":["Defining the problem","Documenting the design process","Testing the effectiveness of a prototype","Drawing a diagram to represent ideas linked to a central keyword"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Brainstorming generates and links many ideas around a central topic, often drawn as a diagram. The other options belong to other stages.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is NOT a method of idea generation?","options":["Free writing","Brainstorming","Digital mapping","Word association"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Free writing, brainstorming and word association are standard idea-generation techniques; 'digital mapping' is not (mind mapping is).","module":"2"},{"q":"Concept formulation is important because it provides","options":["a set of materials to prepare and display ideas","an approach for forming relationships between concepts","a way to make connections and form relationships among peers","an opportunity to explore ideas by making connections between items of information"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Concept formulation lets you explore ideas by connecting pieces of information to build a concept.","module":"2"},{"q":"Oral presentation skills are important in the world of digital media because they<br>I. can enhance marketing skills<br>II. allow for visual representation of data<br>III. can help to communicate complex concepts","options":["I only","I and II only","I and III only","I, II and III"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Good oral skills help market ideas and explain complex concepts; visual representation of data comes from visual aids, not speaking.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following BEST describes the complete creative process?","options":["Designing a solution for two related problems","Taking a problem through to an implemented solution","Taking a problem through to a solution being designed","Taking a solution and retracing how the problem was solved"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. The complete creative process runs from accepting the problem all the way to implementing (and evaluating) the solution.","module":"3"},{"q":"During which stage of the creative process is the individual required to take time to study the problem at hand and how it relates to its various components?","options":["Analysis","Ideation","Evaluation","Implementation"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Analysis means studying the problem and how its parts relate.","module":"3"},{"q":"An entrepreneur is applying the creative process to solve a problem. At which point in the process should he do a mind-mapping chart?","options":["Ideation","Selection","Analysis","Definition"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Mind mapping is an idea-generation technique, so it is used in the ideation stage.","module":"3"},{"q":"After studying and defining the problem, the next step in the creative process is to","options":["sell ideas","accept ideas","generate ideas","evaluate ideas"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. After analysis and definition comes ideation, which is generating ideas.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following terms BEST describes this approach?","passage":"<p>This item refers to the following diagram which shows an approach to the creative process.</p><p><i>Diagram:</i> from <b>Accept situation</b> two arrows lead off. The upper path goes to Analysis, which splits into Ideate and Define. The lower path goes to Define, which splits into Ideate and Re-Analyze; Re-Analyze leads to another Ideate. Every one of these paths ends at <b>Select</b>. Select leads to Implement, which splits into Evaluate and Re-Analyze, and Re-Analyze also points to Evaluate.</p>","options":["Linear","Cyclic","Branched","Feedback"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. The diagram splits into several alternative paths that rejoin later, which is a branched approach.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following is NOT a core preproduction task when doing digital video production?","options":["Logistics","Budgeting","Visual Effects","Storyboarding"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Visual effects are added in post-production; logistics, budgeting and storyboarding are done before filming.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following is an important part of the planning process when preparing to build a website?","options":["Wireframe","Logo design","Dreamweaver","Colour scheme"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. A wireframe maps out the page layout and structure during website planning, before design and building.","module":"3"},{"q":"The arrangement of elements within a user interface or layout is called","options":["use of space","rule of thirds","composition","visual hierarchy"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Composition is the overall arrangement of visual elements in a layout.","module":"3"},{"q":"Michael has developed a mobile application that allows users to search for appropriate shoes at two major online retailers by entering their gender and shoe size.<br><br>Which of the following would NOT be a necessary step in the process of developing this application?","options":["Developing a storyboard and a shot list","Obtaining a price list from a local shoe retailer","Doing a survey to determine the appropriateness of the app","Obtaining a list of all the possible shoe sizes from a local shoe retailer"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. The app only searches two online retailers, so a local retailer’s price list plays no part in developing it.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following is NOT considered part of the five-step approach to the ideation process in developing an inventive solution?","options":["Define","Validate","Generate","Evaluate"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Defining the problem, generating ideas and evaluating them are core ideation steps; validation is not part of this model.","module":"3"},{"q":"A software team is designing a website for a retail clothing store. Which of the following is an important factor to be considered?","options":["PC compatibility","iPad compatibility","Mobile compatibility","Android compatibility"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Many shoppers browse on phones and tablets, so the site must work well on mobile devices generally, not just one platform.","module":"3"},{"q":"What type of targeting should be used to ensure that an advertisement is seen mostly by persons between the ages of 19 and 21?","options":["Contextual","Behavioural","Geographic","Demographic"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Targeting by age is demographic targeting.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following can be used for organizing information between groups of people?","options":["Blog","Wiki","Podcast","Live streaming"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. A wiki lets many users work together to add, edit and organise shared information.","module":"3"},{"q":"Storyboard Pro, Animoto and Wavepad are all","options":["audio players","digital media tools","video editing software","photo editing software"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. They are different kinds of applications for creating media (storyboarding, video creation and audio editing), so the only label that fits all of them is digital media tools.","module":"3"},{"q":"When creating a video of a school's graduation ceremony to be sold to students, which of the following is the BEST format for the final product?","options":[".mpeg2",".jpeg",".wav",".gif"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. MPEG-2 is a video format (used for DVDs); JPEG and GIF are image formats and WAV is audio.","module":"3"}]},{"kind":"p1","id":"DP2018","title":"Paper 01 · 2018","time":90,"intro":"<p><b>CAPE Digital Media Unit 1 Paper 01 · 2018</b> · 1 hour 30 minutes · 50 items</p><p class=\"hint\">Original: the June 2018 computer-based paper (50 items).</p><ol><li>Answer <b>ALL</b> items. Each item has four options lettered (A), (B), (C), (D).</li><li>Start the optional timer to practise under exam conditions.</li><li>Submit to see your score, the key and an explanation for every item.</li></ol>","items":[{"q":"Software that can be used and modified from its original source and sold to other users is BEST described as open","options":["data","source","domain","educational resources"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Open source software has source code that anyone may use, modify and redistribute, including selling it.","module":"1"},{"q":"The term 'bandwidth' refers to","options":["a high-speed Internet connection","the download speed of a connection","the number of IP addresses present in a network","the transmission capacity of a communication line"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Bandwidth is the maximum data transmission capacity of a communication channel.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following techniques allows a user to efficiently share multiple files as a single file across digital platforms?","options":["Email","Upload","File transfer","File compression"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Compression tools such as ZIP bundle many files into one smaller archive for easy sharing.","module":"1"},{"q":"Historically, Web 2.0 tends to refer to a time in the history of the Internet when","options":["Web 1.0 websites started to become less popular","websites began to adopt HTML5 and Javascript","a new version of the web was released by the World Wide Web consortium","interaction and ability for users to add or modify information became more important"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Web 2.0 describes the shift to a participatory web where users create, share and modify content; it was not a formal release by the W3C.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is an open source operating system?","options":["iOS","Android","Windows","Mac OS X"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Android is built on the open source Android Open Source Project and Linux kernel; the others are proprietary.","module":"1"},{"q":"A collection of systems used to protect the copyrights of electronic media is referred to as","options":["a copyright system","trademark registration","digital rights management","copyrights management"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Digital rights management (DRM) is the set of technologies used to control access to and copying of copyrighted digital content.","module":"1"},{"q":"Max is contracted by Skaters International to create an animated logo for use in their marketing campaign using social media marketing. Which of the following describes scanned art work which is further edited and finalized using artistic software?","passage":"<p>This item refers to the drawing canvas shown below.</p><p><i>Picture:</i> a drawing program window with a toolbar of drawing tools down the left side. On the grid canvas is a colour cartoon of a boy in a red helmet, orange shirt and blue jeans doing a trick on a green skateboard.</p>","options":["2D artwork","Animated art","Digitized artwork","Computer generated graphics"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Hand-made art that is scanned into a computer and then refined with software is digitized artwork.","module":"1"},{"q":"On a social networking site, Susan posted a video of herself dancing. Soon, persons started sharing the video link across the Internet. Which of the following ethical issues should be of concern to Susan?","options":["Piracy","Privacy","Plagiarism","Creditability"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Her personal video is spreading beyond the audience she intended, which is a privacy concern.","module":"1"},{"q":"A patent is a set of exclusive rights that protects","options":["an idea","an invention","a common logo","a political slogan"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Patents protect inventions, not bare ideas; logos are protected by trademarks.","module":"1"},{"q":"The combination of emerging technologies, such as robotics, physical science, art and other studies, which produce graphics that can entail gestures and speech, can be classified as","passage":"<p>This item refers to the picture below.</p><p><i>Picture:</i> a photograph of a real street with buildings and parked cars. In front of the scene a hand holds up a torn piece of paper with a pencil line drawing of a bus on it. The drawing lines up with the street behind it, so the sketch and the photograph blend into one image.</p>","options":["2D","3D","digital","hybrid"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Combining several technologies and disciplines, like mixing a drawing with a photograph, produces hybrid graphics.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following file types CANNOT be used as a video format?","options":[".avi",".png",".mpg",".wmv"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. PNG is a still image format; AVI, MPG and WMV are video formats.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following activities could be considered a cybercrime?","options":["Unlocking a mobile phone","Intercepting mobile communication","Saving customer data to a thumb drive","Using a free software to develop an app"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Intercepting other people's communications without authorisation is illegal interception, a cybercrime.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following creation techniques use geometrical primitives such as points, curves, lines and shapes to produce images in computer graphics?","options":["Vector Graphics","Graphics Polarity","Triangular Graphics","Graphics of Digital Media"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Vector graphics are defined mathematically by points, lines, curves and shapes, so they scale without losing quality.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following does NOT present an ethical issue in the field of digital media?","options":["John sharing a video he shot and edited with his friends.","John copying a commercial CD he borrowed from his friend.","John selling a popular movie that he downloaded from YouTube.","John downloading an expensive video editing suite from a file sharing site."],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Sharing his own original video raises no ethical issue; the others involve copyright infringement or piracy.","module":"1"},{"q":"When one does a preliminary version of a film by producing successive sections using storyboard and then add a sound track, this is referred to as","options":["animatics","graphics plot","3D product design","computer generated graphics"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. An animatic is a storyboard played in sequence with a soundtrack to preview the timing of a film.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following processes must be completed immediately before an end user is able to purchase a new device?","options":["Creation","Production","Distribution","Certification"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. After a device is created and produced, it must be distributed to retailers before end users can buy it.","module":"2"},{"q":"Brainstorming is BEST for idea","options":["analysis","evaluation","generation","implementation"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Brainstorming is a technique for generating many ideas quickly without judging them.","module":"2"},{"q":"The process of idea generation encourages","options":["criticism","limited ideas","outlandish ideas","the discarding of ideas"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Idea generation defers judgement and welcomes wild or unusual ideas to increase creativity.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following statements are TRUE about venture capitalists?<br>I. They only fund large businesses.<br>II. They provide equity for businesses.<br>III. They expect high returns on their investments.","options":["I and II only","I and III only","II and III only","I, II and III"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Venture capitalists invest money in exchange for equity and expect high returns; they often fund small, high-growth start-ups rather than only large businesses.","module":"2"},{"q":"The stakeholder is MOST likely the","passage":"<p>This item refers to the following value chain.</p><p><i>Diagram:</i> five boxes joined by arrows, left to right: Content Creation → Aggregation &amp; Publishing → Distribution (Fixed &amp; Mobile) → Customer Environment → Stakeholder.</p>","options":["customer","programmer","content creator","content distributor"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. The stakeholder sits at the end of the chain after the customer environment, so it is the customer who consumes the content.","module":"2"},{"q":"How does globalization impact the digital media expansion?","options":["It balances it","It slows it down","It accelerates it","It doesn't impact it"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Globalization opens worldwide markets and audiences, which speeds up the growth of digital media.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following are parts of a project proposal?<br>I. Objectives<br>II. Project duration<br>III. Expected results","options":["I and II only","I and III only","II and III only","I, II and III"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. A project proposal sets out its objectives, the duration and the expected results.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following persons is MOST likely a digital native?","options":["Your mother or father","Your 40 years old teacher","Your 10 years old sibling","A 50 years old computer repairman"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. A digital native grew up surrounded by digital technology, which fits the youngest person.","module":"2"},{"q":"Omar wants to seek funding for his business proposal. The banking sector does not want to take the risk of providing funding. What is the BEST alternative source of funding for his business proposal?","options":["Savings","Credit union","Stock market","Crowdfunding"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Crowdfunding raises money from many people online without needing a lender to accept the risk.","module":"2"},{"q":"As a digital media practitioner, which of the following may BEST enhance employability?","options":["Accounting practices","Building a presentation","Dressing appropriately","Developing a personal portfolio"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. A personal portfolio shows employers real evidence of a digital media practitioner's skills and work.","module":"2"},{"q":"Paul decides to open a business that designs websites; however, he needs to seek financing. The financial institution requires him to provide a detailed business plan, an expected cash flow statement, an asset liquidity position, and collateral. What type of financing is Paul seeking?","options":["Debt","Equity","Grant","Company"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Collateral and cash-flow evidence are required when borrowing a loan, which is debt financing.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following terms BEST describes the emergence of worldwide markets?","options":["E-commerce","Globalization","Internationalization","Geographical information"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Globalization is the integration of national economies into worldwide markets.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is NOT a method of idea generation?","options":["Free writing","Brainstorming","Digital mapping","Word association"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Free writing, brainstorming and word association are standard idea-generation techniques; 'digital mapping' is not (mind mapping is).","module":"2"},{"q":"When measuring environmental challenges and opportunities, context is usually measured as","options":["outer and inner","local and global","personal and public","individual and mutual"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Environmental scanning considers the context at local and global levels.","module":"2"},{"q":"Oral presentation skills are important in the world of digital media because they<br>I. can enhance marketing skills<br>II. allow for visual representation of data<br>III. can help to communicate complex concepts","options":["I and II only","I and III only","II and III only","I, II and III"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Strong oral presentation helps sell ideas and explain complex concepts; visual representation of data comes from visuals, not speaking skills.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following BEST describes the complete creative process?","options":["Designing a solution for two related problems","Taking a problem through to an implemented solution","Taking a problem through to a solution being designed","Taking a solution and retracing how the problem was solved"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. The complete creative process runs from accepting the problem all the way to implementing (and evaluating) the solution.","module":"3"},{"q":"During which stage of the creative process is the individual required to take time to study the problem at hand and how it relates to its various components?","options":["Analysis","Ideation","Evaluation","Implementation"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Analysis means studying the problem and how its parts relate.","module":"3"},{"q":"Anila is designing an interactive map for her school’s website and wants to highlight multiple locations on the map. Which of the following software would be BEST for implementing the map?","options":["Photo editing","Movie editing","Mind mapping","Online mapping"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Online mapping tools such as Google My Maps let you place and highlight several locations on an interactive map.","module":"3"},{"q":"The arrangement of elements within a user interface or layout is called","options":["use of space","rule of thirds","composition","visual hierarchy"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Composition is the overall arrangement of visual elements in a layout.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following elements is MOST important for enhancing entrepreneurial skills?","options":["Constant learning","Adequate finance","Professional certification","Social accommodation"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Skills improve through ongoing learning; finance and certification do not in themselves build entrepreneurial skill.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following is NOT a core preproduction task when doing digital video production?","options":["Logistics","Budgeting","Visual effects","Storyboarding"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Visual effects are added in post-production; logistics, budgeting and storyboarding are done before filming.","module":"3"},{"q":"A software team is designing a website for a retail clothing store. Which of the following is an important factor to be considered?","options":["PC compatibility","iPad compatibility","Mobile compatibility","Android compatibility"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Many shoppers browse on phones and tablets, so the site must work well on mobile devices generally, not just one platform.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following is an important part of the planning process when preparing to build a website?","options":["Wireframe","Logo design","Dreamweaver","Colour scheme"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. A wireframe maps out the page layout and structure during website planning, before design and building.","module":"3"},{"q":"When using a PowerPoint file for a public presentation, which of the following describes the background for the slides?","options":["Simple color scheme","Calming artistic photo of a landscape","Any type of photo related to the content","Exciting and colorful image that keeps attention"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. A simple colour scheme keeps text readable and does not distract the audience from the content.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following steps is first in the creative process?","options":["Selection","Interaction","Acceptance","Creative cognition"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. The creative process begins with accepting the situation (the problem) before analysing it.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following are methods of implementing the creative process?<br>I. Linear<br>II. Square<br>III. Cyclic","options":["I and II only","I and III only","II and III only","I, II and III"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. The creative process can be followed in a linear or cyclic way; square is not a recognised approach.","module":"3"},{"q":"What type of targeting should be used to ensure that an advertisement is seen mostly by persons between the ages of 18 and 21?","options":["Contextual","Behavioural","Geographic","Demographic"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Age is a demographic characteristic, so demographic targeting is used.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following can be used for organizing information between groups of people?","options":["Blog","Wiki","Podcast","Live streaming"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. A wiki lets many users work together to add, edit and organise shared information.","module":"3"},{"q":"Storyboard Pro, Animoto and Wavepad are all","options":["audio players","digital media tools","video editing software","photo editing software"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. They cover storyboarding, video creation and audio editing, so the only common category is digital media tools.","module":"3"},{"q":"When creating a video of a school's graduation ceremony to be sold to students, which of the following is the BEST format for the final product?","options":[".mpeg2",".jpeg",".wav",".gif"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. MPEG-2 is a video format (used for DVDs); JPEG and GIF are image formats and WAV is audio.","module":"3"},{"q":"At what stage of the production process will the above chart/graph/illustration be referred to?","passage":"<p><i>Diagram:</i> a cycle of six circles linked by arrows: product → optimize → markets → research → strategy → biz dev → back to product. In the middle are four coloured blocks labelled media, technology, audience and impact.</p>","options":["Before pre-production","Pre-Production Only","Post-Production only","Both in Pre-Production, and Post Production"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. The cycle covers planning (research, strategy) and evaluating results (optimize, markets), so it is used both in pre-production and post-production.","module":"3"},{"q":"When text is to be added to video production, this is done sometimes at the end of the production, though it can be done at other points. When the text is added to the end of the production of a video, this is referred to as:","options":["Texting","Closing Words","Captions","Credits"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Text at the end of a video listing the people involved is called the credits.","module":"3"},{"q":"The above icons are used to carry out what important task in video editing?","passage":"<p><i>Picture:</i> two small toolbar icons from a video editing program. The first shows a bar with a vertical marker separating a filled (blue) section from an empty section. The second shows a filled (blue) section held between two vertical markers, with empty sections outside them.</p>","options":["Remove excess sound from a production","Remove sections of video or sound that is not required for production","Add extra video footage to a production being created in video editing","Modify sections of a video before finalising production"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Split and trim tools cut clips so unwanted portions of video or sound can be removed.","module":"3"},{"q":"What is the highlighted box below in Windows Movie Maker referring to?","passage":"<p><i>Picture:</i> a screenshot of Windows Live Movie Maker. On the left is the preview window showing horses running on a beach under the title “Wild Horses”. On the right a purple box highlights the panel where the project’s video clips and title cards (“Wild”, “Directed by”, “Starring”) are laid out in order as a row of thumbnails.</p>","options":["Effects","Timeline","Transitions","Plug-ins"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. The highlighted area shows the clips arranged in order, which is the timeline (storyboard) where the video is assembled.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following stages of the creative process is associated with the user consulting with peers or supervisors regarding insights before pursuing the project further?","options":["Acceptance","Definition","Ideation","Evaluation"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Evaluation involves reviewing progress and getting feedback from peers or supervisors to judge whether to continue.","module":"3"}]},{"kind":"p1","id":"DP2020b","title":"Paper 01 · 2020","time":90,"intro":"<p><b>CAPE Digital Media Unit 1 Paper 01 · 2020</b> · 1 hour 30 minutes · 45 items</p><ol><li>Answer <b>ALL</b> items. Each item has four options lettered (A), (B), (C), (D).</li><li>Start the optional timer to practise under exam conditions.</li><li>Submit to see your score, the key and an explanation for every item.</li></ol>","items":[{"q":"Software that can be used, modified, and sold to other users is BEST described as","options":["Open data","Open source","Open domain","Educational resources"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Open source software has freely available source code that users may use, modify and redistribute, including commercially.","module":"1"},{"q":"The term ‘bandwidth’ refers to","options":["a high-speed internet connection","the download speed of a connection","the number of IP addresses present in a network","the transmission capacity of a communication line"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Bandwidth is the maximum data transmission capacity of a communication channel.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following does NOT present an ethical issue in the field of Digital Media?","options":["John sharing a video he shot and edited with his friends","John copying a commercial CD he borrowed from his friend","John selling a popular movie that he downloaded from YouTube","John downloading an expensive video suite from a file sharing site"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. John owns the video he created, so sharing it raises no ethical issue; the others involve copyright infringement.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which file format is BEST suited to this image? <i>(The original item prints no question stem under the picture; this line is added by Kester Small.)</i>","passage":"<p>This Item refers to the following picture.</p><p><i>Picture:</i> two photographs side by side, joined by an arrow pointing from the left one to the right one. Each shows the black silhouette of a galloping horse against a yellow background above a dark strip of ground; the horse’s legs are in a different position in each frame, so together they form a short motion sequence (animation).</p>","options":["JPEG","GIF","EPS","TIFF"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. GIF supports multiple frames, so it can store simple looping animations like the galloping horse; JPEG, EPS and TIFF are still-image formats.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is an open source operating system?","options":["iOS","Android","Windows","Mac OS X"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Android is built on the open source Android Open Source Project and Linux kernel; the others are proprietary.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is achieved through the sensitive balance of variety and unity in colour?","options":["Tint","Neutral","Shading","Harmony"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Colour harmony is the pleasing arrangement of colours that balances variety (interest) with unity (order).","module":"1"},{"q":"A body of practical knowledge which provides guidance in colour mixing while noting the visual effects of colour combinations is called colour","options":["Theory","Mixing","Patching","Arrangement"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Colour theory is the body of guidance on mixing colours and on the visual effects of colour combinations.","module":"1"},{"q":"Susan logged into a social networking site and posted a video of herself dancing. Soon, persons started sharing the video link across the internet. Which of the following ethical issues should be of concern to Susan?","options":["Piracy","Privacy","Plagiarism","Creditability"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Her personal video is spreading beyond the audience she intended, which is a privacy concern.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is the MOST recent mode of live event streaming accepted by companies and individuals?","options":["Podcast","Webcast","YouTube","Infographics"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. A webcast broadcasts a live event over the internet; podcasts are pre-recorded and infographics are static graphics.","module":"1"},{"q":"The mixture of a colour with black to reduce the lightness is called","options":["Hue","Tint","Shade","Tint shade"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Adding black to a colour creates a shade; adding white creates a tint.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following file types CANNOT be used as a video format?","options":[".avi",".png",".mpg",".wmv"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. PNG is a still image format; AVI, MPG and WMV are video formats.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following activities could be considered a cybercrime?","options":["Unlocking a mobile phone","Intercepting mobile communication","Using a free software to develop an app","Opening customer data stored on a thumb drive"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Intercepting other people's communications without authorisation is illegal eavesdropping, a cybercrime.","module":"1"},{"q":"Max is contracted by Skaters International to create an animated logo for use in its social media marketing campaign. Which of the following describes scanned artwork which is further edited and finalized using artistic software?","passage":"<p>The item refers to the drawing canvas shown below.</p><p><i>Picture:</i> a drawing program window. A toolbar of drawing tools (pen, eraser, fill, line, rectangle, ellipse, text, eyedropper and a stroke setting) runs down the left side; on the grid canvas is a coloured cartoon of a boy in a red helmet, orange shirt and blue jeans riding a green skateboard.</p>","options":["2D artwork","Animated art","Digitized artwork","Computer generated graphics"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Artwork drawn by hand, scanned into a computer and then finished in software is digitized artwork.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following is MOST important in digital media and the internet?","options":["Material discovery","Dynamic discussion","Raising social issues","Raising ethical issues"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. The internet's core value in digital media is enabling people to discover and access material (content) easily.","module":"1"},{"q":"The act of acquiring digital content to be used in production is called","options":["Capturing","Researching","Collating","Collecting"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Capturing is the process of acquiring digital content such as photos, video or audio for use in a production.","module":"1"},{"q":"Which of the following processes must be completed immediately before an end user is able to purchase a new device?","options":["Creation","Production","Distribution","Certification"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. After a device is created and produced, it must be distributed to retailers before end users can buy it.","module":"2"},{"q":"Paul decides to open a business that designs websites; however, he needs to seek financing. The financial institution requires him to provide a detailed business plan, an expected cash flow statement, an asset liquidity position, and collateral. What type of financing is Paul seeking?","options":["Debt","Equity","Grant","Company"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Collateral and cash-flow evidence are required when borrowing a loan, which is debt financing.","module":"2"},{"q":"The process of idea generation encourages","options":["Criticism","Limited ideas","Outlandish ideas","The discarding of ideas"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Idea generation defers judgement and welcomes wild or unusual ideas to increase creativity.","module":"2"},{"q":"Oral presentation skills are important in the world of digital media because they<br>I. can enhance marketing skills<br>II. allow for visual representation of data<br>III. can help to communicate complex concepts","options":["I only","I and II only","I and III only","I, II and III"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Good oral skills help market ideas and explain complex concepts; visual representation of data comes from visual aids, not speaking.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is NOT needed to enhance entrepreneurship in the digital media industry?","options":["Programming","Continuous learning","Portfolio development","Ability to market ideas"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Continuous learning, a portfolio and marketing ability are key entrepreneurial assets; programming is a technical skill not essential to every digital media entrepreneur.","module":"2"},{"q":"The stakeholder is MOST likely the","passage":"<p>This item refers to the following value chain</p><p><i>Diagram:</i> five boxes joined by arrows, left to right: Content Creation → Aggregation &amp; Publishing → Distribution (Fixed &amp; Mobile) → Customer Environment → Stakeholder.</p>","options":["Customer","Programmer","Content creator","Content distributor"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. The stakeholder sits at the end of the chain after the customer environment, so it represents the customer who consumes the content.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following are parts of a project proposal?<br>I. Objectives<br>II. Project duration<br>III. Expected results","options":["I and II only","I and III only","II and III only","I, II and III"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. A project proposal sets out its objectives, the duration and the expected results.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following activities BEST describes the process of brainstorming?","options":["Defining the problem","Documenting the design process","Testing the effectiveness of a prototype","Drawing a diagram to represent ideas linked to a central keyword"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Brainstorming generates and links many ideas around a central topic, often drawn as a diagram. The other options belong to other stages.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following devices can be used to capture video?<br>I. Tablet PC<br>II. Smartphone<br>III. Graphics Tablet","options":["I and II only","I and III only","II and III only","I, II and III"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Tablet PCs and smartphones have built-in cameras; a graphics tablet is a pen input device with no camera.","module":"2"},{"q":"Omar wants to seek funding for his business proposal. The banking sector does not want to take the risk of providing funding. What is the BEST alternative for his business proposal?","options":["His savings","Credit union","Stock market","Crowdfunding"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Crowdfunding raises small amounts from many people online, avoiding traditional lenders who see the idea as too risky.","module":"2"},{"q":"How does globalization impact the digital media expansion?","options":["It balances it.","It slows it down.","It accelerates it.","It does not impact it"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Globalization opens worldwide markets and connections, speeding up the growth of digital media.","module":"2"},{"q":"Concept formulation is important because it provides","options":["a set of materials to prepare and display ideas","an approach for forming relationships between concepts","a way to make connections and form relationships among peers","an opportunity to explore ideas by making connections between items of information"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Concept formulation lets you explore ideas by connecting pieces of information to build a concept.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following is NOT a method of idea generation?","options":["Free writing","Brainstorming","Digital mapping","Word association"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Free writing, brainstorming and word association are standard idea-generation techniques; 'digital mapping' is not (mind mapping is).","module":"2"},{"q":"Steven wants to start a music production business and requires a total of $100 000. [He has $50 000] in savings and his brother invests $25 000. He then acquires a $25 000 loan from the bank to make up for the total amount.<br>This type of funding can be BEST described as","options":["debt","equity","debt and equity","venture capital"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Savings and his brother's investment are equity, while the bank loan is debt, so the funding is a mix of both.","module":"2"},{"q":"Which of the following may BEST enhance the employability of a digital media practitioner?","options":["Accounting practices","Building a presentation","Dressing appropriately","Developing a personal portfolio"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. A personal portfolio showcases a practitioner's skills and work to prospective employers and clients.","module":"2"},{"q":"The creative process ends at the step known as","options":["ideation","analysis","definition","evaluation"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Evaluation is the final stage, where the implemented solution is reviewed against the goals.","module":"3"},{"q":"During which stage of the creative process is the individual required to take time to study the problem at hand and how the problem relates to its various components?","options":["Analysis","Ideation","Evaluation","Implementation"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. Analysis involves studying the problem and how its parts relate before generating ideas.","module":"3"},{"q":"Anila is designing an interactive map for her school’s website and wants to be able to highlight multiple locations on the map. Which of the following software would be BEST for implementing the map once it is created?","options":["Photo editing","Movie editing","Mind mapping","Online mapping"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Online mapping tools (such as Google My Maps) let users place multiple interactive markers and embed the map in a website.","module":"3"},{"q":"Digital media tools have a significant and continuously changing impact on","options":["Politics","Ecology","The economy","Education"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Digital media constantly reshapes the economy by creating new industries, business models and jobs.","module":"3"},{"q":"A software team is designing a website for a retail clothing store. Which of the following is an important factor to be considered?","options":["PC compatibility","iPad compatibility","Mobile compatibility","Android compatibility"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Many shoppers browse on phones and tablets, so the site must work well on mobile devices generally, not just one platform.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following is NOT a core preproduction task when facilitating digital video production?","options":["Logistics","Budgeting","Lighting","Storyboarding"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Lighting is set up and adjusted during production; logistics, budgeting and storyboarding are planned in preproduction.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following terms BEST describes this approach?","passage":"<p>This item refers to the following diagram which shows an approach to the creative process.</p><p><i>Diagram:</i> from <b>Accept situation</b> two arrows lead off. The upper arrow goes to <b>Analysis</b>, which splits to <b>Ideate</b> and to <b>Define</b>; both point to <b>Select</b>. The lower arrow goes to <b>Define</b>, which splits to <b>Ideate</b> (pointing to Select) and to <b>Re-Analyze</b> → <b>Ideate</b> (pointing up to Select). <b>Select</b> → <b>Implement</b>, which splits to <b>Evaluate</b> and to <b>Re-Analyze</b>; Re-Analyze also points to Evaluate.</p>","options":["Linear","Cyclic","Branched","Feedback"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. The process splits into multiple alternative paths that later rejoin, which is a branched approach.","module":"3"},{"q":"Kiara created a game to be played on mobile devices. It can be downloaded free of cost but upgrades for added features have to be purchased. This is known as a","options":["civic app","public app","freemium app","commercial app"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. Freemium apps are free to download but charge for premium features or upgrades.","module":"3"},{"q":"Marcus Banton is a graduate of a local high school in your country. He recently created an innovation for mobile phones. It is anticipated that sales in the mobile phone market will jump by over 43 per cent in the upcoming 18 months. Armed with this information, Marcus is concerned about selling his idea to manufacturers without getting any lifetime rewards for his invention. Which intellectual property will cover his invention and what lifetime reward he should seek?","options":["Copyright, Return and Investment","Patent, Royalty","Trademark, Share of Profit","Industrial Design, Rights to company shares"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Inventions are protected by patents, and licensing a patent earns the inventor ongoing royalties on each sale.","module":"3"},{"q":"The first step in the creative process is","options":["selection","interaction","acceptance","creative cognition"],"answer":2,"why":"Key: C. The creative process begins with accepting the situation (acceptance) before analysis and definition.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following can be used for organizing information between groups of people?","options":["Blog","Wiki","Podcast","Live streaming"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. A wiki lets many users work together to add, edit and organise shared information.","module":"3"},{"q":"What type of targeting should be used to ensure that an advertisement is seen mostly by persons between the ages of 18 and 21?","options":["Contextual","Behavioural","Geographic","Demographic"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. Age is a demographic characteristic, so demographic targeting is used.","module":"3"},{"q":"Which of the following terms accurately defines the overlay of black lines in the picture above?","passage":"<p>This item refers to the following picture.</p><p><i>Picture:</i> a photograph of a Rottweiler leaping towards the camera over grass, with a concrete wall behind it. Two evenly spaced horizontal black lines and two evenly spaced vertical black lines are drawn over the photo, dividing it into nine equal rectangles; the dog’s head sits near the upper-left crossing point.</p>","options":["Depth of field","Rule of thirds","Stop motion photography","Shutter speed"],"answer":1,"why":"Key: B. Two horizontal and two vertical lines dividing the frame into nine equal parts form the rule of thirds grid.","module":"3"},{"q":"The MAIN rationale for the Creative Process in Digital Media is that","options":["innovators are encouraged to provide new products, service including hardware and software that can create economic welfare and sustain small-business development","a wealth of resources are provided solely for online usage","the potentials of the human brain to think digitally is maximized","small business are created for the benefits of those living solely in small communities and Caribbean states"],"answer":0,"why":"Key: A. The creative process drives innovation in products and services that generate economic welfare and sustain small businesses.","module":"3"},{"q":"At what stage(s) of the production process would the diagram above be referred to?","passage":"<p>This item refers to the following diagram</p><p><i>Diagram:</i> a central square of four coloured blocks labelled <b>media</b>, <b>technology</b>, <b>audience</b> and <b>impact</b>, surrounded by six circles linked by arrows running clockwise in a cycle: product → optimize → markets → research → strategy → biz dev → back to product.</p>","options":["Before preproduction","Preproduction Only","Postproduction only","Both in Preproduction and post production"],"answer":3,"why":"Key: D. The cycle covers planning (research, strategy) and post-release activities (optimize, markets), so it is referred to in both preproduction and postproduction.","module":"3"}]}]);
